{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong","id":55030,"title":"3e Abyssals Are Dark Solars (A Conversation From The TVTropes Forum) (Warning: LOONG)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-21T16:37:03-08:00","id":55030,"title":"3e Abyssals Are Dark Solars (A Conversation From The TVTropes Forum) (Warning: LOONG)","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I've been browsing the dev commentary on 3E and I have to say....I am...underwhelmed...with the look of Abysaals so far.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The changes to Resonance bother me, I can understand </span></span><i>why</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> it is often put upon/dissed, but personally speaking I like it the way it is, since it helps to quantify the Abysaal condition- which is one of utter despair. The whole point of being a Death Knight is that you accept complete death in exchange for a half life- a half life that is </span></span><i>enforced</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> both by that acceptance and by the control exerted by the Death Lords, the Neverborn, and beyond that the Void itself. The Abysaals are all about hopelessness, about having to face mortality and the inevitability of one's own demise, of the demise of all things, and of the nature of death. In many ways- making them the most </span></span><i>human</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> Exalted. They are confronted with an inescapable reality, and unlike Solars who can just ignore it and Infernals who can just give it the bird, they </span></span><i>must</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> face it- sooner or later, either through succumbing to despair and embracing it becoming murder happy nhillist psychos, finding solace and purpose in other areas of death (like the Exalted who acts a minster/diplomat from ghosts to the living), or struggling with it- every day to find some sort of way to cope with these realities while subject to the whims and terrors of the Death Lords.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Or, maybe, ever once and so rarely....Turning on those self same Deathlords- and fighting against all odds to break free of their shackles, to find a true meaning and understanding from existence, wrest from the throws of death a life: such a quest that can take them to only one place at the end. The maw of Oblivion, to confront the Neverborn themselves.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I don't know...It feels like the death and hopeless angle is being...abandoned in favor of drifting back to &quot;Dark Solars&quot; more and more- which is....less interesting to me. I feel like Infernals fill the slot of dark/twisted Solars a lot better (but then I also feel like the state of Infernal and Abysaal end games should be reversed- and Infernals should have the chance for redemption while Abysaals should be unable to switch back in their life times) and that Abysaals have a lot of potential to be the mirror of the Solars in a different way then just &quot;Solars that glow black&quot;. The Solars are all about life and living- about seizing every moment and taking every challenge, climbing ever mountain, the Abysaals should be all about death, about facing grim reality and tragedy, about being confronted with hopelessness and despair and a dark fate, and maybe- just maybe- finding hope there, and telling the Neverborn to blow it out their undead asses.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I also, am not a fan of the idea of Deathlords being responsible for the creation of Abysaal Exaltation, VS the Neverborn- since it really does sort of neuter the whole narrative strength of Abysaals. The Deathlords as they are- glorified inreaibly powerful insane Dragons to the </span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BigBad\" target=\"_blank\">Big Bad</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> of the Neverborn makes the most sense, and a big point of the Abysaals </span></span><i>is</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> that they are made painfully clearly aware that the </span></span><i>Neverborn</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> insane and lost in nightmares of the void as they are are the end game. They stand at the precipitate of the void, the edge of nothingness, they are ancient and twisted and impossible and they want </span></span><i>everything</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> to die, and they are using you to do it. Shifting the focus to the Deathlords serves as another narrative barrier, takes away a little bit (A lot) of the punch of a Abysaal endgame- </span></span><i>going to the maw</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">, facing this long dead ghosts of their makers, the very symbolic source of this hopelessness and malice attached to their condition- to death, and beating them, beating it.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I just...I feel like Abysaals are going to loose a lot of their draw- for me personally- when we see The Void and the Darkness fall into the background, while focus on the Death Lords, and being &quot;Dark Solars&quot; comes to the fore.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rikalous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">As their Storytelling chapter notes, Infernals don't really </span></span><i>need</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> redemption, because they don't have Resonance slapping them down every time they try to do straightforward heroics outside of the Underworld.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I </span></span><i>really</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> don't want to derail into another Infernals discussion, but I will state, to me, that Infernals and Abysaal represent very different things.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Abysaals are opposite of Solars their dark mirror, while Infernals are Solars twisted. The endgame for Abysaals shouldn't be redemption, because they are the ones who don't need it (And it always felt bitter in my mouth, especially if you run with the Abysaals-as-metaphor-for-depression, in which case &quot;Redemption&quot; defeats the whole point- which is learning to live with death and inevitability of it, learning to live with their demons and push forwards anyways- and instead just being like &quot;flip a switch and suddenly everything is awesome and better&quot;) while Infernals, who represents twisted Solars rather then their opposite, who's whole arc is based around and beings with Fucking Up Royaly (TM) and cutting a deal to make things better, hell who had they done differently </span></span><i>would</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> have been glowing gold (Remember- Abysaals are chosen not by fate but by the insane death lords, who Exalt almost at random) and really, their end game should be moving past that, or overcoming it in someway, which narratively would be best concluded with becoming a Solar- earning the Exaltation that should have been theirs to begin with etc.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">(If our local Infernal fanboy wouldn't fry the living hell out of me- I would so house rule Abysaals as non-redemptive and Infernals as redemptive. But I might actually be the first person to be punched through an internet screen if I did.)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ira The Squire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">And here's the problem: one of the shticks of Exalted is about being awesome and heroism, which makes this kind of take really out of place.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">If you want despair, play Vampire</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Who says you can't be awesome and heroic while facing utter despair? (To me- that's the best kind of heroism, courage in the face of unquestionable, unrelenting </span></span><i>doom</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">. Going in, without a chance, without hope and still fighting anyways- and maybe just maybe...If all the winds blow fair all the Stygia stars line up right...winning.)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ira The Squire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">That's not the type of heroism that Exalted is going for: Exalted is about </span></span><i>winning</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> no matter the circumstances. It's not about standing up even when you are definitely going to lose: it's about winning even when you are sure you're going to lose. Thus things like the Primordial War where you do things that are impossible, Perfect defences which blocks things that are supposed to kill you 100%. It's not about heroism or courage during a</span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HopelessWar\" target=\"_blank\">Hopeless War</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> or </span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DefiantToTheEnd\" target=\"_blank\">Defiant to the End</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">If you want that type of heroism or courage, that's a </span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/NewWorldOfDarkness\" target=\"_blank\">New World of Darkness</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> thing, not Exalted.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Meh. I am of the opinion that the majority of mechanics should be treated as a strong suggestions anyways.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">That having been said- simply abandoning that angle all together by completely ditching Resonance and overhauling all the themes and ideas of the Abysaals isn't the answer. The primary theme of the Abysaal splat was dealing with death and it's inevitability, just like the central theme of the Core Solars is living life against all odds- the Abysaals all show a myriad of ways (and the splat allows for a ton more) to deal with this condition- and that's </span></span><i>fascinating</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> and </span></span><i>interesting</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">. But with by just ditching Resonance, completely reformatting the Deathlord/Abysaal relationship, hell even altering the </span></span><i>source</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> of the Exaltation, they are tossing out the baby with the bathwater.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">EDIT: And why not? Why can't that be the Abysaal's specific flavor of heroism? Every other Exalted gets their own specific style of the heroic and their own themes to build off of- and I'm not saying the Abysaal's shouldn't be able to accomplish the impossible- in fact I firmly believe that the Abysaal's story leads to once place- overthrowing the Neverborn and closing the Maw of the Void- so the Underworld can be liberated from the Abyss and they can turn it into something </span></span><i>good</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Finding hope and joy and new rebirth in death- that's where the Abysaal story should lead. &quot;Dark Solars&quot; feels like a cop out- and more over feels like doubling down on what we already have for that- the Infernals.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ira The Squire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Because it goes against a theme that is common with every other splat (There's nothing mechancially stopping other splats except Infernals from fixing things, and Infernals have their own mechanics to get them out from the mechanics that stops them from fixing things)? And against the themes of the rest of the game? There is a reason why the backstory have the Primordial War, after all. Also, if Abyssals are supposed to be about </span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DefiantToTheEnd\" target=\"_blank\">Defiant to the End</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> why let them have Perfects at all? Point of Perfects is to show that even against odds that seem like suicidal the Exalted will still win.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Also, Resonance mechanically make what you suggest about fighting the Neverborn </span></span><i>impossible</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">, simply because it just undoes everything that you do. It is the worst of </span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ResetButton\" target=\"_blank\">Reset Button</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rikalous</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The impression I got from the dev commentary is that the changes to Resonance and the deathlord/Abyssal relationship were about providing greater freedom within the splat. Without Resonance slapping you down every time you defend or become friends with someone living, there's now room for Abyssal characters who aren't grimloner or evil to go forth and adventure through all the cool stuff in Creation. Without the default assumption that Abyssals are slaves, runaway or otherwise, to the deathlords Abyssals are free to have adventures where their deathlord isn't a major overhanging threat. To analogize across to other splats, they've also talked about how even though barbarianism is a major theme for Lunars a socialite Lunar will be totally viable, and even though Getimians are apparently linked to this rogue Sidereal warring against heaven, one of the sigs is apparently working as a special consultant for them.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">And the thing is, if you want to have the old stories, there's really nothing stopping you. Want your deathlord to keep sending dudes to kill you? You're free to include backstory where you pissed them off and now they dearly want your skull for a drinking cup. Want to do a story where hopelessness is the Abyssal condition? You can still have their attempts at heroics lead to awfulness and failure, you just have to do it with the story instead of the mechanic.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">And I firmly believe that none of the splats should only have one place their story can lead.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Only it doesn't? Each Exalted has it's specific central themes that have very little to do with each other- and while there are a lot &quot;core&quot; themes, what I've said about Abysaals.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Exalted's central theme is- you can do the impossible. But no where does it say that you </span></span><i>will</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> do the impossible, or that the impossible will be easy. (And yes- the game does have serious problems with power scale at times, but I honestly don't get the impression, especially from Dev comments that these epic feats of awesome are supposed to be easy.) More over, Exalted is a pointless exercise if everything is easy- no victory has meaning if it's just simply won.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">As for Perfects- those come with flaws recall? And even if they didn't- they are more a mechanical balancing agents against insane damage or </span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DVs\" target=\"_blank\">D Vs</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> then they are serious thematic aspect.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">As for Resonance, dealing with it isn't impossible: and any prereq story to confronting the Neverborn will undoubtedly have to feature an arc where the Abysaals learn to temper it- which makes for an interesting challenge and chance to develop the characters, as well as a good story on it's own.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I want say the Resonance is without problems- I think with a GM in the right mind set not exactly insurmountable problems- but there are problems. But the idea of Resonance is vital to creating the &quot;all odds against&quot; &quot;hopeless despair&quot; element that features into such a grim and macabre Exalt. That isn't to say hopelessness and despair can't be overcome- but to me at least, the overcoming of that, and the making peace with death itself, through overthrowing the Neverborn and their agenda, or finding a sense of purpose in a different cause, or even whatever, that should be the end game of the Abysaals. Coming to terms with Death, and even changing it's very nature if they wish to try.</span></span> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">For the sake of clarification: When I say &quot;one place&quot;, I mean metaphorically- that is, peace with Death- in whatever form that takes. To me ideally that form would be overthrowing the Neverborn and repairing the Maw, so the Death Knights can transition into rulers/protectors of the Underworld. To some it might be fostering relations between dead and living, or trying to reconnect with family and friends in the after life, or maybe just being left alone to do whatever it is they do.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Unless you want to play a murder happy psychopath- in which case more power to you.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ira The Squire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I am of the opinion that </span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WhiteWolf\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> have a habit of making their systems that is the opposite of what the game they want needs. A narrative-focused game should not have mechanics getting in the way of story progression to where it is supposed to go.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">As written, you cannot foster good relations between the living and the dead as an Abyssal. At some point you will have to compromise to the living and technically that counts as defending the living from death. Then Resonance erupts and the living dies. And also as written the Abyssal cannot rebel against the Neverborn </span></span><i>at all</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> without almost immediate Resonance eruption.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Count Dorku</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">If your GM is splitting hairs that finely, it is not the fault of the mechanics.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">(This is not saying that I like standard Resonance - I </span></span><i>vastly</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> prefer the one in Shards - but that sounds more like a GM issue than anything inherent to the rules.)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The thing is- when you change the landscape so utterly, along side the build it just becomes a different beast. The Death Lord/Abysaal relationship becoming more Master/Apprentice and less antagonistic wouldn't be terrible on it's own- it would still shake things up- but they are completely ditching Resonance, hell even changing the </span></span><i>source</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> of Abysaal Exaltation's construction from Neverborn to Deathlord. They are stripping down the things that contain the themes and ideas central to the Abysaal story and condition- in favor of moving them away from the void and that story into being &quot;Dark Solars&quot;- which is both incredibly boring as an idea and really annoying since the game has </span></span><i>so much</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> Solar focus already.</span></span> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">That's a bit of a dick move on the </span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GMs\" target=\"_blank\">G Ms</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> part and less a fault with the mechanics.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Count Dorku</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I love the way that literally every single complaint I have heard about every single change that is being made to every single splat has involved a comparison to Solars.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I'm not </span></span><i>surprised</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">, because this has been going since 3e was announced, but I </span></span><i>am</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> getting </span></span><i>incredibly</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> tired of it.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Well....IT's hard to deny, that the game is becoming vastly more Solar-centric. I'm not fan of Infernals but even I raise an eyebrow in changing them to be &quot;commentary on the Solar's decadence&quot; rather then the trans-humanist whatevers they where before. (Which given that I am kind of extremely allergic to their whole tranhumanism combined with unabashed objective [still hate that word] evil, should say how worrying the change should be.)</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">But seriously, this:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">&quot;&quot;Dark Solars&quot; continues to be a concept that fires my imagination, far more than &quot;Exalt of the [Oblivion/Void/other generic concept]&quot; ever will, and that the game has pushed them in that direction in 2e is one of the number one reasons why they went from arguably the most popular splat in 1e to the hands-down least popular splat in 2e.&quot;&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Is not okay.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Count Dorku</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The Abyssals were always &quot;Dark Solars&quot;, dude. Their original conception...well, okay, their original conception was </span></span><i><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/VampireTheMasquerade\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Masquerade</a></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">, but when translated into the Exalted setting it was &quot;Dark Solars&quot;. 1e was Dark Solars. 2e was Dark Solars Who Suck And Get Set On Fire When They Try To Not Suck. 3e may actually be making them </span></span><i>less</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> Dark-Solars, because for a change their Charmset is not going to be loaded with &quot;this works just like Solar Charm X&quot; and &quot;Solars have Charm Y which works exactly like that&quot;.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Also, I will note that everyone </span></span><i>warned you</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> that chapters 1 and 2 of MOXP: Infernals did not represent any view of the subject matter that led to good gameplay or the ability to relate to them, and you read them anyway.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God of Awesome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Mechanically, they are becoming less Dark Solar.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Thematically? I also think the same as with mechanics. Solars start off almost practically on their own. Abyssals will be Princes Of The Underworld, given what I understand, with more positive relationships with fuck motherin' </span></span><i>Deathlords</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Honestly, Abyssals are starting to sound like </span></span><i>Goth Infernals</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">While Infernals are starting to sound like Hell Solars.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I don't get why everyone is so freakin down on 2e Abysaals- the game as a whole has a serious problem of entitlement and silver-spoon syndrome among the majority of the Exalted. Abysaals where the ones trying to actively subvert that- there is no special criteria to become one, they are stacked with odds that just might posse a real conflict driven threat, and they are written with such amazing imagery and themes in regards to death and dying, particularly in the Exalted setting where the potential exists not only for them to change the entire game re: The Nature of Death but it is actively assumed they will do so- at the same time the obstacles they face aren't ones that can just be crushed with some cunning minimaxing and rules lawyering. They require a real story- an epic world spanning earth shattering story that is </span></span><i>hard</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> and full of struggle and loss and pain- but the glorious ending is still within reach, and always a possibility if you are simply brave enough and stubborn enough to keep trying.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">And, I feel like all that great potential is just going to get tossed out, or at the very least left by the way side and completely neutered in favor of making them more generic &quot;Dark Solars&quot;. I actually don't mind the mirrored Charm sets, and honestly I would take their being a near mechanic carbon copy as long as their unique flavor was preserved. What bothers me is and will always be the story of it.</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">As for Infernals- It's not just the first few chapters that make me decidedly un-interested in them. (Though make no mistake- they are truly disgusting...And I will note still have the glowing endorsement of the Devs.) It's also the kind of completely disjointed transhumanism themes that pushes an already over the top setting so far over the top that it's insane into completely unreasonable territory. (Though in the spirit of fairness- I can understand the draw of that and the logic behind it I just....I am not a fan.)</span></span> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">RE: GoA: I can't even begin to express the sheer annoyance this fills me with.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Then the conversation meanders into a discussion over game theory. This topic resurges but I won't quote it. The beginning of this conversation starts <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/posts.php?discussion=i49lv2deedw2ynrskgyhwt2h&amp;page=86\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. After the conversation on Kung Fu Panda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:58:33-08:00","id":55038,"title":"","content":"For one thing, Abyssals don't confront their mortality. That's what gets them Exalted in the first place. <br /> <br /> For another, Ex2 Abyssals were very much designed as Black Solars and the narrative and mechanics pushed them to attain redemption and become Solars (read: <i>real</i> Exalts). That's the problem with Mirror charms and the way Ex2 handled Resonance.<br /> <br /> I don't understand how anyone could look at Ex3 Abyssal spoilers and think they're being made more into Black Solars than they already, even if that were possible. The spoilers we've had so far very clearly emphasize the differences between Solars and Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T17:18:16-08:00","id":55051,"title":"","content":"I was just kinda going along politely disagreeing with LMage. I blinked in confusion at how he somehow got the impression that not only are Abyssals meant to change the nature of death but that doing so in a fairly particular way is <i>inevitable</i>. I did likewise with similar interpretations that don't line up with anything I've seen. I kinda presumed he just really wanted something other than what seems to be coming down the pipes.<br /> <br /> Just... don't have much to say. Those are some nice diverging opinions and probable big misconceptions?<br /> EDIT: Did post a quote about laughing hysterically at the &quot;glowing endorsement of the Devs&quot; line -- which I did indeed do -- but realized immediately after posting he probably meant about Infernals, not &quot;the first few chapters.&quot; So, I disagree, but I'll be respectful enough not to assume he's completely ignorant about how nigh-universally those chapters are loathed, especially among the EX3 Team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 01-21-2014, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:46:11-08:00","id":55105,"title":"","content":"I pretty much disagree with LMage about most of what he says. My biggest draw to Exalted is that nothing is inevitable. At no times are you stuck with the lot you're given. Abyssals are Dark Solars. They shouldn't be a mirrored clone of the Solars, but they are most definitely what happens when you take a Solar Exaltation and taint it with death. The Deathlords can control the Abyssals no more than the Yozi can control their Princes. I like the idea of redemption, and plan to have an Abyssal go that route one day, but that shouldn't be your only choice beyond accepting everything your Deathlord tells you to do. That's the problem with 2e Abyssals: They were shackled. Here are your Black Solar Charms and here are your orders. You want out? Okay, go be a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:05:15-08:00","id":55156,"title":"","content":"Who the hell cares how the authors wrote them in the books. you want &quot;dark solars&quot;, run them that way. if you want &quot;servants of the deathlords&quot;, run them that way. if you want &quot;harbingers of oblivion&quot;, run them that way. Me, i'm gonna do &quot;all of the above&quot; because i realize that a splat comes with far more than just a single theme built in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:07:42-08:00","id":55158,"title":"","content":"Me think LMage should just play WoD if he like despair and inevitable while having your face being stomp on by your Elder so much. I can't take him seriously when he's trying to make 3rd Abyssal look bad by calling them &quot;Dark Solar&quot;. And what with this &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">transhumanism&quot; and &quot;body horror&quot; that some anti-Infernal fan </span></span>keep going about, every Yozi charmtree only have like 2 or 3 charms that involve growing organic brass from your skin or all your command UMI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:38:51-08:00","id":55178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=55158#post55158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me think LMage should just play WoD if he like despair and inevitable while having your face being stomp on by your Elder so much. I can't take him seriously when he's trying to make 3rd Abyssal look bad by calling them &quot;Dark Solar&quot;. And what with this &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">transhumanism&quot; and &quot;body horror&quot; that some anti-Infernal fan </span></span>keep going about, every Yozi charmtree only have like 2 or 3 charms that involve growing organic brass from your skin or all your command UMI.</div> </div> </div> </div> And not a damned thing wrong with transhumanism as a theme. considering that's where our own society is rapidly heading, it's as fine a time as any to explore its possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:49:47-08:00","id":55185,"title":"","content":"I think that whatever happens to 3E Abyssals, I hope they have more flexibility. They are traditionally the <i>only</i> Exalts of the Underworld: A spiritual realm with a population that eclipses that of Creation. In such a setting, having them shackled to one singular purpose (murder Creation) is doing the very potential of their existence a massive disservice. I think the &quot;murder Creation&quot; thing should be part of who they are, but not to the exclusion of everything else. &quot;Princes of the Underworld&quot; makes a great deal more sense and is a better reflection of their relationship to the Deathlords. The Deathlords are all technically supposed to be working towards the end of all things and, sure, some of them are. But some of them are content to preserve the status quo because they enjoy their position of power and privilege. Who wouldn't? Abyssal students of these figures would in all likelihood have some similar attitudes towards the fate of the Underworld. It makes a lot of sense for <i>most</i> Abyssals to not be obsessed with destroying all things; maybe they're preoccupied with murdering entire cities to bring them into the Underworld and thereby enhancing its wealth and prestige, but they know to draw a line lest they accidentally suck all of the Underworld down the drain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:57:12-08:00","id":55194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=55185#post55185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that whatever happens to 3E Abyssals, I hope they have more flexibility. They are traditionally the <i>only</i> Exalts of the Underworld: A spiritual realm with a population that eclipses that of Creation. In such a setting, having them shackled to one singular purpose (murder Creation) is doing the very potential of their existence a massive disservice. I think the &quot;murder Creation&quot; thing should be part of who they are, but not to the exclusion of everything else. &quot;<b>Princes of the Underworld</b>&quot; makes a great deal more sense and is a better reflection of their relationship to the Deathlords. The Deathlords are all technically supposed to be working towards the end of all things and, sure, some of them are. But some of them are content to preserve the status quo because they enjoy their position of power and privilege. Who wouldn't? Abyssal students of these figures would in all likelihood have some similar attitudes towards the fate of the Underworld. It makes a lot of sense for <i>most</i> Abyssals to not be obsessed with destroying all things; maybe they're preoccupied with murdering entire cities to bring them into the Underworld and thereby enhancing its wealth and prestige, but they know to draw a line lest they accidentally suck all of the Underworld down the drain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last time this come up, those who want to play the above archetype got told that they really just want to play Goth Solar.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:07:36-08:00","id":55200,"title":"","content":"I would love to play as a Goth Solar if I could figure out a way to deal with all the sunlight and being endorsed by the King of Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:27:57-08:00","id":55219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=55194#post55194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The last time this come up, those who want to play the above archetype got told that they really just want to play Goth Solar.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>By who?<br /> <br /> (more characters so it's more than 10)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:39:49-08:00","id":55227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=55219#post55219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By who?<br /> <br /> (more characters so it's more than 10)</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Underworld Lord&quot; guy make quite a fuss so it's a only thing that I remembered from that horrendous Abyssal theme thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:41:44-08:00","id":55228,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, there's been a few of those, about a bunch of different things regarding Abyssals. Any more info you can remember?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:42:02-08:00","id":55229,"title":"","content":"Ah. I was afraid you were talking about someone important. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T21:47:20-08:00","id":55231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=55200#post55200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to play as a Goth Solar if I could figure out a way to deal with all the sunlight and being endorsed by the King of Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the traditional meaning of &quot;Goth&quot; would be really easy to do with that, as it had more to do with finding beauty in situations that others wouldn't, among other things. F'rex, being able to admire the Grave Hound's ability to consume the flesh of the dead, and give them a chance to finish something that was holding them from Lethe.<br /> <br /> The more commonly used version, however....<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Well, there's another version of &quot;Goth&quot;, but Rome doesn't exist, so you'd really just end up pissed off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T22:01:44-08:00","id":55245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=55228#post55228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, there's been a few of those, about a bunch of different things regarding Abyssals. Any more info you can remember?</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>&quot;Just take Vile Anathema Shroud ! Tada, now your Solar can play Underworld Lord while Abyssal can be world-killing weapon.&quot;</li> <li>It's a Fitter Happier thread so it's not only boring but it's got worse fast, and FH misinterpreted everyone posts as usual.</li> <li>Someone talking about Abyssal having the shackle of the Neverborn on their shoulder is super thematic or something.</li> <li>Thought most of the thread just involve Mr.Insecure and Fitter Happier arguing about Abyssal theme AKA &quot;Abyssal shouldn't be Oblivion's bitch&quot; vs &quot;Abyssal should be Oblivion's bitch&quot;.</li> </ul>That's all I remembered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T23:19:07-08:00","id":55276,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with Abyssals being the harbringers of inevitable death. What I <i>do</i> have a problem with is when they enforce that theme by having the Neverborn literally smack you down if you try to act outside that theme. That's just crude, and more than a little silly. A better implementation would be to offer temptations: The Abyssal charmset is death-themed, and they are at their strongest when acting as harbringers of death. It's not that they <i>can't</i> run a kingdom without Shadowlands randomly popping up and disgorging nephwracks all over Creation, but they're so much <i>better</i> at commanding with the dead that they're always tempted to gradually turn their kingdom into a thanatocracy. The 2e charmset looked like it was paying lip service to that idea, but in the worst possible way: Most of the Abyssal charms were just &quot;Do exactly what Solars do, but with <i>murder!</i>&quot; (or, worse yet, &quot;Do exactly what Solars do, but with <i>creepy flavor text!</i>&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T23:41:49-08:00","id":55293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=55276#post55276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(or, worse yet, &quot;Do exactly what Solars do, but with <i>creepy flavor text!</i>&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I liked the &quot;identical Charm except with creepy flavor text&quot; thing. Then again, I also liked just the Solar flavor text. Have you read Door-Evading Technique recently? Genius!<br /> <br /> But I guess it all depends on whether you're OK with the Abyssal Charms being funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T06:36:35-08:00","id":55417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drakhan Valane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=55219#post55219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By who?<br /> <br /> (more characters so it's more than 10)</div> </div> </div> </div>People who want Abyssals to be designated bad guys all day erryday.<br /> <br /> And Fitter Happier. Who I exempt from the others largely due to his frickin' metal Resonance Rewrite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T08:30:39-08:00","id":55460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=55417#post55417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People who want Abyssals to be designated bad guys all day erryday. And Fitter Happier. Who I exempt from the others largely due to his frickin' metal Resonance Rewrite.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like to use them as badguys, because realistically, they were the only other exalted type that could come close to challenging the solars on their own level, aside from infernals. But at the same time, i dont want them to be one dimensional. i want there to be a great amount of variations in the goals and motivations for the deathknights. to those in creation, abyssals are the enemy, plain and simple. they work for the deathlords, who are known to slaughter entire cities and drag whole lands down into the shadow. the average citizen (even exalted) doesnt want anything to do with that. however if one were to examine the actions of the deathknights closer and from the perspective of the citizens of stygia and the deathcults residing within the shadowlands, you would find a differing opinion of them, something more akin to the awe afforded to the heroes of creation. and that should rightfully confuse and frustrate those who see them nothing more than &quot;evil gothic solars&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T08:58:25-08:00","id":55483,"title":"","content":"The best villains are the ones you can relate to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T09:13:08-08:00","id":55495,"title":"","content":"As I've said in past Abyssal threads, there's nothing is wrong with having some Abyssals who want to end the world, act as Deathlord slaves, and are chained to Oblivion. There is a problem when all of that is mandatory for <i>every</i> Abyssal, with the only other choice being, turn into a Solar. It also, as Tobi mentioned, doesn't do justice to the Underworld, which is a massive place with a lot more room for themes and concepts than, &quot;Oblivion.&quot; <br /> <br /> The writers have been clear that 3rd edition Abyssals will be different from older ones in terms of themes and mechanics, and they have pointed people towards early First Edition material (the corebook and the Storyteller's Companion) for ideas of where they would like to take Abyssals.<br /> <br /> For the people who were big fans of 2nd edition Abyssals, they can always run Exalted using 2nd edition Abyssals (sort of like how I imagine fans of 2nd edition Infernals will be porting them into 3rd edition). <br /> <br /> AnubisXy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:15:44-08:00","id":55566,"title":"","content":"Some more stuff that what got brought up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God of Awesome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Although, one thing I think about now in disagreement to </span></span><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/LMage\" target=\"_blank\">L Mage</a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Abyssals, despite their visual aesthetics, aren't really metaphors for depression, they're metaphors for </span></span><i>fear</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">.</span></span><br /> <i>Infernals</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">, to me, make better metaphors for depression.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LMage</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">....Elaborate. Please.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God of Awesome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Abyssals became what they are because they were afraid of dying. Strong depression leads to suicide but for the Abyssals that was the opposite of what they did. They had </span></span><i>so much to live for</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">, just living at the very least. &quot;I am </span></span><i>afraid</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> of dying.&quot; Now they run and hide and clench their heads, these horrible fucking </span></span><i>anxious </i><b>Whispers</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> in their head and this constant overhanging shadow, this incomprehensible horrible </span></span><i>thing</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> looking over their shoulder, just waiting for murder everybody.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I mean, it </span></span><i>can</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> get pretty depressing, it should really. Anxiety, fear, depression, IIRC, that's all some linked stuff. But originally, it the Abyssal's curse sprung from fear.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Infernals </span></span><i>suck</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">. That's why they're Infernals. Now they got hookers and blow to cover it all up and make the hurt go away, just for a second, until realityozi comes crashing down with a horrible hang over.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Of course, there is a lot of crossover, everything Abyssals touch is much more at risk of becoming tainted than Infernals. But yeah, Infernals are chosen cause they screwed up, and no one wants to be a screw up. Abyssals are chosen because they were </span></span><i>afraid</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">And because the Lion or whoever liked the cut of his jib that morning.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Now, you said earlier, you though the Redemption/Evolution path should be reverse for the Solaroids, because depression-metaphor Abyssals don't just snap, a-ha, I'm no loner depressed. It works better for the Infernals then, slowly evolving, </span></span><i>transcending</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">, beyond the chains that held them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">While Abyssals.... okay, I dunno, how the fuck does dealing with phobias, anxiety and paranoia work?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Count Dorku</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;I dislike death, but there are things I dislike more than death, therefore there are occasions on which I will not avoid danger.&quot;</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> - Master Meng (Latinized as Mencius)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The stereotypical phobia therapy would be exposure treatment - gradually learning to face your fears, rather than back down from them. Having the psychiatric qualifications of a small table, though, I can't say whether it works or not.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">In the overall metaphor, that would be renegade Abyssals repeatedly coming face to face with their own potential deaths, enduring the hunt of their former colleagues - running up against the forces of death time and again - and eventually they realise: they're not afraid of it any more. If it comes down to dying, or watching others die, they'll hurl themselves in the way of a blade, smiling as they do so.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">And </span></span><i>that</i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> is the moment golden light flares, and the Neverborn tremble in the depths of the Labyrinth.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God of Awesome</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>fuck yeah</i></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:54:04-08:00","id":55590,"title":"","content":"People have been pretty good about this so far, but in the interest of not creating cross-forum drama could we please not single out the posts of who aren't on this forum to argue their case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T12:20:13-08:00","id":55607,"title":"","content":"Well, I did ask LMage before posting.<br /> <br /> Not the other people though but they hadn't been saying anything inflammatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome"