tps://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:04:26-08:00","id":56404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gatts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56371#post56371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, that sounds like an Ebon Dragon debating charm-tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be really glad when 2e has been out of cycle for years and no one remembers its interpretation of the Ebon Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:18:48-08:00","id":56495,"title":"","content":"Amen.<br /> <br /> Nothing against Infernal fans but 2e Fiends steal everything cool Abyssals should have. Right down to one of their frigging Caste marks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T20:23:24-08:00","id":56552,"title":"","content":"Finally in Ex3 my Fiend can peacefully be a Goth without people keep calling him for a Vamp or Emo. Though I do like stealing Midnight's caste mark though ;D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T20:37:36-08:00","id":56556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56495#post56495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amen.<br /> <br /> Nothing against Infernal fans but 2e Fiends steal everything cool Abyssals should have. Right down to one of their frigging Caste marks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm? If the Ex3 Ebon Dragon is going to be anything like the Ex1 Ebon Dragon, they're going to persist in dwelling in the dark and flirting with the edge of death, and they;re going to do it even harder than in Ex2. The difference is that they're attracted to what will pass and don't actually want to have a twilight realm of doom and gloom ruled by the dead, because they get off on a clear difference between the quick and the deceased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T22:50:45-08:00","id":56592,"title":"","content":"So basically this Ira the Squirrel is saying all splats should feel and play the same.<br /> <br /> Pardon my french, but this person's argument is retarded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:55:57-08:00","id":56759,"title":"","content":"I have to say that I like Abyssals to be doomed. I like that they start out as weapons with no choice but to murder the world - willingly through their actions or unwillingly through Resonance. What I don't like is that the story ends there. The Abyssals are too doomed. There are no escape clauses in their contract except for redemption into a Solar. They can't branch out.<br /> <br /> Strangely, the best example of how doomed I want them to be is Elsa from Disney's Frozen. She's got powers and they are destructive to everyone around her - she freezes the whole country into eternal winter on accident and almost kills her sister. However, she kept it together for years practicing discipline and in the end manages to figure out how to control it completely. In the meantime, those powers are wonderful and useful - she builds a massive ice castle in a matter of moments. Now, she gets off a little easy - it is a Disney movie after all - but that's sort of what I hope Abyssals can be - people with at least a third option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T09:01:37-08:00","id":56805,"title":"","content":"The &quot;third option&quot; is a very attractive idea, but as an end state it's destructive to (my preferred interpretation of) Abyssal themes because it makes redemption superfluous. If you have the option to avoid your doom and remain an Abyssal, there is no argument to be made that being an Abyssal is something you need to redeem yourself of. The scrupulous and disciplined Abyssal isn't taking a third option in my view -he's taken some steps that are necessary for redemption, but hasn't gone far enough (and might not be willing to go to the required lengths, if he sees himself as having paid his dues already.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","user":"Schleiermacher","date":". 01-24-2014, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T09:30:26-08:00","id":56822,"title":"","content":"I feel like this whole &quot;fight with the disagreeable conditions of Abyssal Exaltation&quot; deal is a leftover from Vampire. A very dangerous leftover that francly feels terribly out of place in Exalted. When I'm playing an epic hero in a game of romance, war and adventure, going &quot;o woe is me, for I am deeeeaaaad&quot; all the time is just tedious. I have better things to do.<br /> <br /> Besides, I really fail to see how are Abyssals more doomed then Solars, considering the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> Edit: Don't get me wrong- I love the theme of fighting against the inevitable like any other guy, but I feel like it's an experience that can be explored by any PC in any RPG. Making it a core of the Abyssal game kinda prohibits other splats on that, because that's basically THE thing the Abyssal game has going for it. I want to be able to play a Solar figthing against losing odds, thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-24-2014, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T10:09:16-08:00","id":56846,"title":"","content":"Honestly that part's kind of what irritates me about Solars. Abyssals get a poor escape clause, and the entire set of circumstances requiring them to have it need to change, but it's still an escape clause. Infernals and Alchemicals get them too (both handled much better than the one for Abyssals), I've always been annoyed that the others don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T10:42:10-08:00","id":56869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56805#post56805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have the option to avoid your doom and remain an Abyssal, there is no argument to be made that being an Abyssal is something you need to redeem yourself of.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the crux of an Abyssal player's conundrum. He wants to play an <i>Abyssal</i><i>,</i> not a Solar. Otherwise, he would have skipped playing an Abyssal and played a Solar. So, from a playability perspective, Abyssals must be a splat that you can play without being forced to turn into another splat. A player should not feel bad or punished for playing an Abyssal instead of a Solar.<br /> <br /> I think we need to change what we mean when we talk about &quot;redemption&quot; for Abyssals. The &quot;sin&quot; that an Abyssal needs redemption from is not being an Abyssal. Their &quot;sin&quot; is agreeing to kill the world. An Abyssal can be a tempted being, more able to solve problems with indiscriminate murder, but if he wants to recant on that promise without becoming a Solar, the game should let him. Sure, make him take the hard road. Deny him some of the most effective tools. Let his Deathlord see him as a traitor to the cause (or maybe not - some of the Deathlords really don't want Creation gone). Have him bear some pain for denying the purpose for which he was created. Just don't make him go gold instead of black.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T10:42:55-08:00","id":56870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56822#post56822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this whole &quot;fight with the disagreeable conditions of Abyssal Exaltation&quot; deal is a leftover from Vampire. A very dangerous leftover that francly feels terribly out of place in Exalted. When I'm playing an epic hero in a game of romance, war and adventure, going &quot;o woe is me, for I am deeeeaaaad&quot; all the time is just tedious. I have better things to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's merit in the idea that the different exalted splats ought to be based around different themes and core stories. If playing an Abyssal lets you tell the exact story of romance, war, and adventure that you can get with a Solar, then why have Abyssals?<br /> <br /> Vampires are popular (for White Wolf and in pop culture in general) because lots of people like 'o woe is me, for I am deeeeaaad.' The idea of noble but tragic monsters/anti-heroes is appealing. <br /> <br /> I agree that sometimes Exalted has done this to excess in 2nd Edition, but I recall Abyssals being a fan favorite in 1st Edition specifically because playing the dark, vampiric Exalted was seen as more fun than the vanilla Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T11:03:52-08:00","id":56881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56870#post56870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If playing an Abyssal lets you tell the exact story of romance, war, and adventure that you can get with a Solar, then why have Abyssals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, to me that kind of sounds like, &quot;If using a sword lets you stab people just as effectively as a spear, then why have spears?&quot; Some people like variety and the fact that the two different exalt types play differently enough, even if their stories can be similar, doesn't mean that we shouldn't have a particular exalt type.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T11:18:31-08:00","id":56888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56870#post56870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's merit in the idea that the different exalted splats ought to be based around different themes and core stories. If playing an Abyssal lets you tell the exact story of romance, war, and adventure that you can get with a Solar, then why have Abyssals?<br /> <br /> Vampires are popular (for White Wolf and in pop culture in general) because lots of people like 'o woe is me, for I am deeeeaaad.' The idea of noble but tragic monsters/anti-heroes is appealing.<br /> <br /> I agree that sometimes Exalted has done this to excess in 2nd Edition, but I recall Abyssals being a fan favorite in 1st Edition specifically because playing the dark, vampiric Exalted was seen as more fun than the vanilla Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but playing the dark, vampiric Exalted is very different then playing a slave to both an oppresive master and inevitable fate, you know. I don't believe that vampire is popular because people like &quot;woe is me, for I am deeeaaad&quot;. I think that what people expect from experience of playing a vampire-like creature is very much opposite to what we got- freedom.<br /> <br /> Like, when I think vampires, I don't think &quot;emo people crying themselves to sleep because they're deeeeaaaad&quot;. I think proud and powerful creatures of the night, regal and mysterious, towering over mortals with just how fucking scary but alurring they are. But what we get, is a huge load of limitations. I think it's bad. Needless to say, I wasn't especially impressed with Requiem and it's weird insistance that being a vampire is inherently problematic and it's basically a downgrade. I <i>hate</i> that idea.<br /> <br /> So, honestly, I think the direction the Devs are taking- making Abyssals into those regal figures of undead authority, basically free to carve their own path, but having a very heavy incentive to work under a powerful Lord- is the best direction they could have taken. And in the process they're also making Abyssals play meaningfully different. And if you want to have an emo experience I think that Abyssals are still best for that without limitting the game experience to only that.<br /> <br /> I am a little afraid of the whole setting going too Solar-centric, because the entire Universe serving as a commentary on just those 150 guys just rubs me the wrong way, but in all the sea of awesome, that's a rather silly bone to pick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-24-2014, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T11:27:09-08:00","id":56893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56881#post56881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, to me that kind of sounds like, &quot;If using a sword lets you stab people just as effectively as a spear, then why have spears?&quot; Some people like variety and the fact that the two different exalt types play differently enough, even if their stories can be similar, doesn't mean that we shouldn't have a particular exalt type.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason to use a sword over a spear or a spear over a sword if they're mechanically the same, which is why they're not mechanically the same in many RPGs.<br /> <br /> If we had an entire book dedicated to sword fighting and an entire book dedicated to spear fighting, then them being the same save for some aesthetics would be a let down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:41:12-08:00","id":56934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56893#post56893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason to use a sword over a spear or a spear over a sword if they're mechanically the same, which is why they're not mechanically the same in many RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a very good reason: I like the way it looks and prefer it over the other options. In Exalted, aesthetics can matter a lot depending on the player and their character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:49:27-08:00","id":56945,"title":"","content":"I always thought the idea that Abyssals were Undead Solars and therefore EVIL was kind of below Exalted, which is a cleverer game of that.<br /> <br /> Abyssals should be to Hades like the Solars are to Zeus, that is to say, champions of divine power with no moral stricture coming along with that.<br /> <br /> There should never, ever be any rules which impose an ethical state along with Exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T14:13:34-08:00","id":57001,"title":"","content":"Let's go about this from another angle:<br /> <br /> I want to play an Exalted character.<br /> <br /> I want this character to live in the Underworld and respire its deathly Essence. I want to wield Charms and Sorcery that are death-themed and that are focused on decay and horror. I want to use and wear magical material that gives me bonuses but that is dark in colour and quality (not bright and shiny). I also don't want to have to waste bonus points on unnecessary Mutations or Hearthstones to achieve this aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Should I play as a Solar, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T14:14:18-08:00","id":57002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56945#post56945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should never, ever be any rules which impose an ethical state along with Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say this is not exactly true. There are a few things that humans generally agree are wrong - the most common being that killing another person for the reason of personal gain. Abyssals, during their Exaltation, must agree to kill the entire world in order to save their own lives and gain power. Depending upon how wholeheartedly they must agree, every Abyssal starts with a pretty black stain on their soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T14:33:48-08:00","id":57012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57002#post57002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say this is not exactly true. There are a few things that humans generally agree are wrong - the most common being that killing another person for the reason of personal gain. Abyssals, during their Exaltation, must agree to kill the entire world in order to save their own lives and gain power. Depending upon how wholeheartedly they must agree, every Abyssal starts with a pretty black stain on their soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, most of them will start with a hell of an integrity boost- they've just cheated death and it didn't even notice they're selling bullshit to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-24-2014, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T15:10:25-08:00","id":57023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57001#post57001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's go about this from another angle:<br /> <br /> I want to play an Exalted character.<br /> <br /> I want this character to live in the Underworld and respire its deathly Essence. I want to wield Charms and Sorcery that are death-themed and that are focused on decay and horror. I want to use and wear magical material that gives me bonuses but that is dark in colour and quality (not bright and shiny). I also don't want to have to waste bonus points on unnecessary Mutations or Hearthstones to achieve this aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Should I play as a Solar, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm. Obviously. Like, those are Night Caste, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Chaka wrote:<br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1224-drakhan-valane","name":"Drakhan Valane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1224_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T15:48:48-08:00","id":57043,"title":"","content":"Fair points but if were wanting something other then whats presented in the book... we suddenly find a large amount of source material that is WORTHLESS to the game we are wanting to run.<br /> <br /> that is why people who want &quot;Slaves of oblivion&quot; and &quot;righteous champions of the ancestors&quot; And &quot;Tearful Penitents Trying to cleanse their exaltions of the Unholy Necromatic darkness&quot; go at each other so often.<br /> <br /> Every page devoted to ones preferred interprutation of the splat, is a page WASTED to the others POV.<br /> <br /> Personally<br /> <br /> Yes I want to Conquer my curse, atone for the moment of weakness that led me to commit an unspeakable crime and atone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T15:55:22-08:00","id":57046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57012#post57012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, most of them will start with a hell of an integrity boost- they've just cheated death and it didn't even notice they're selling bullshit to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I meant about &quot;how wholeheartedly they must agree&quot; to the deal. If you can say yes and not mean it, then yeah, Oblivion's a chump and the Abyssal hasn't done anything wrong. However, if they have to at least be willing to do it to spare their own life or gain power, then they have a black spot on their soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T16:13:03-08:00","id":57054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57046#post57046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I meant about &quot;how wholeheartedly they must agree&quot; to the deal. If you can say yes and not mean it, then yeah, Oblivion's a chump and the Abyssal hasn't done anything wrong. However, if they have to at least be willing to do it to spare their own life or gain power, then they have a black spot on their soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noooope they don't. I mean, we can be all metaphysical, but I fail to see what a &quot;black spot on the soul&quot; actually means. I remind you that Creation has no concept of &quot;sin&quot;. Agreeing to kill the world might make you feel guilty. Or it might not. It depends entirely on your culture and upbringing. But as itself, it has no real wight to it whether you actually meant it or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T17:57:56-08:00","id":57110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57054#post57054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noooope they don't. I mean, we can be all metaphysical, but I fail to see what a &quot;black spot on the soul&quot; actually means. I remind you that Creation has no concept of &quot;sin&quot;. Agreeing to kill the world might make you feel guilty. Or it might not. It depends entirely on your culture and upbringing. But as itself, it has no real wight to it whether you actually meant it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on one's personal views, neither does the Real World (and even if they do, the concept is pretty mutable). And yet the idea of a black stain on someone's soul is hardly unknown or beyond understanding. So I'm not sure what you're saying, beyond &quot;no one is going to care at all that they/someone else devoted themselves to killing the world&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T18:16:25-08:00","id":57123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=56869#post56869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the crux of an Abyssal player's conundrum. He wants to play an <i>Abyssal</i><i>,</i> not a Solar. Otherwise, he would have skipped playing an Abyssal and played a Solar. So, from a playability perspective, Abyssals must be a splat that you can play without being forced to turn into another splat. A player should not feel bad or punished for playing an Abyssal instead of a Solar.<br /> <br /> I think we need to change what we mean when we talk about &quot;redemption&quot; for Abyssals. The &quot;sin&quot; that an Abyssal needs redemption from is not being an Abyssal. Their &quot;sin&quot; is agreeing to kill the world. An Abyssal can be a tempted being, more able to solve problems with indiscriminate murder, but if he wants to recant on that promise without becoming a Solar, the game should let him. Sure, make him take the hard road. Deny him some of the most effective tools. Let his Deathlord see him as a traitor to the cause (or maybe not - some of the Deathlords really don't want Creation gone). Have him bear some pain for denying the purpose for which he was created. Just don't make him go gold instead of black.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard this before, but I've never understood it. No, you shouldn't be forced to turn into a Solar. And you shouldn't feel punished for playing an Abyssal instead of a Solar. But why do you need moral validation of your character's decision to remain an Abyssal, in order to enjoy playing an Abyssal? I don't think you should get that.<br /> <br /> The sin that an Abyssal needs redemption for is their assent to killing the world. But being an Abyssal is inextricable from that. If someone recants and says &quot;I won't be a world-destroying weapon anymore&quot; ...then if they walk that path to the end there's no way to continue to be an Abyssal, and they shouldn't even want to, because that's absolutely core to what an Abyssal is. Trying to &quot;repent&quot; without abandoning that path is like wanting to be a vegetarian without giving up bacon. When you say &quot;Yes, give me the Second Breath and I will kill the world&quot; the decision you make is not &quot;enlisting as a soldier for the cause of Oblivion&quot;. Sure, the Neverborn would prefer if you were on task, you'd be more efficient that way, but ultimately what is asked of you, and what you agree to, is becoming an Abyssal. It's the nature of the Black Exaltation: Will ye or nill ye, death shall ye cause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noooope they don't. I mean, we can be all metaphysical, but I fail to see what a &quot;black spot on the soul&quot; actually means. I remind you that Creation has no concept of &quot;sin&quot;. Agreeing to kill the world might make you feel guilty. Or it might not. It depends entirely on your culture and upbringing. But as itself, it has no real wight to it whether you actually meant it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point isn't how you feel about it, or what you &quot;meant&quot;. The point is that you agreed to become an Abyssal, and now you are one, and that means you bring death and entropy wherever you go. The guy who thinks &quot;Ha, I totally played that Deathlord! I didn't <i>mean</i> it!&quot; is like the fledgling vampire who thinks &quot;Well, I'm not a sadistic psychopath like those other vampires! <i>I'm</i> not going to be a blood-drinking predator!&quot; Good luck with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T20:07:10-08:00","id":57176,"title":"","content":"Oh god, it's night of the living thread all over again, people has argued Abyssal's theme and bargain to dead and I'm pretty sure nothing good ever come out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T20:28:26-08:00","id":57188,"title":"","content":"You know how I pointed out that this seemed to be a recurring thing every time this subject was brought up? Yeah, this is inevitably what happens. Goddamit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T20:41:52-08:00","id":57198,"title":"","content":"What would you have me do? Someone is Wrong On The Internet! ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T21:43:58-08:00","id":57227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57198#post57198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you have me do? Someone is Wrong On The Internet! ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the devs pointed out that (at least in 3E) Deathknights can do all kinds of things in the Underworld independent of the Deathlords (which doesn't really contribute to destroying Creation), and also that Abyssals who regret their decision can turn against the Deathlords without any kind of redemption whatsoever, (with the mentality that they're damned but they can still protect what they care about by destroying other damned). Yes, obviously, it is a bad thing to agree to destroy Creation, and Abyssals are fundamentally tainted by Oblivion, but that doesn't really mean that they have to be world destroyers since you can destroy things that threaten the world too, and it doesn't even mean they have to be destroyers, since Oblivion can be expressed in ways besides MURDER EVERYONE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1658-maelstromseeker","name":"maelstromseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T22:09:42-08:00","id":57245,"title":"","content":"I do hope that Abyssal charm will be more like Verdant Emptiness Endowment and Golden Years Tarnished Black, you can either be a gigantic douche with them or be the most awesome psychiatrist ever, your choice. Compare to 2ed Abyssal charms which make sure you can only make everybody life sucks as hard as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T23:52:22-08:00","id":57282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57110#post57110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on one's personal views, neither does the Real World (and even if they do, the concept is pretty mutable). And yet the idea of a black stain on someone's soul is hardly unknown or beyond understanding. So I'm not sure what you're saying, beyond &quot;no one is going to care at all that they/someone else devoted themselves to killing the world&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, people are surely gonna care that they agreed to kill the World, I'm sure everybody will be totally convinced of the &quot;black spot&quot; you're talking about. But, just like in real life, it has no meaning because people aren't accauntable for their intentions, but for their actions. I see no reason why an Abyssal shouldn't laugh in the face of anybody who spases out over an imaginary thought-crime the Abyssal allegedly commited. So I really wouldn't like if the book spent pages, upon pages of content focusing on it and explaining how it's a Big Deal, when it's really not, the way Requiem spends way too many pages reminding you that life of a vampire sucks, when it should be awesome in it's own, special way.<br /> <br /> This whole idea &quot;Abyssal's purpose is murder and murder only&quot; is just mind-boggling. When I want to play a machine, I'm gonna play an Alchemical. And I'll have more freedom. There really is a better way of making people end up playing a bloodthirsty psychopaths then just forcing them to, don't let White Wolf convince you otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57123#post57123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard this before, but I've never understood it. No, you shouldn't be forced to turn into a Solar. And you shouldn't feel punished for playing an Abyssal instead of a Solar. But why do you need moral validation of your character's decision to remain an Abyssal, in order to enjoy playing an Abyssal? I don't think you should get that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, what moral validation? Don't push your morals down my throat man, if death asks me whether I will agree to kill the World for a second chance and I say yes, then it's really not your business whether it makes me guilty or not, so stop pushing this guilt and this &quot;sin&quot; on me. Jesus, just because you said something once doesn't mean you have to gloom over it forever.<br /> <br /> That's exactly the thing I hated about 2e Abyssals and it's not even becoming a bloodthirsty psychopath that bothers me, because I can get behind that, it's that I don't feel awesome while doing it. And that's the point- even if the game hinges on my realization that I will become a bloodthirsty psychopath at some point, then I want to have an incentive to do so, instead of being forced to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-25-2014, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T00:36:16-08:00","id":57293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57123#post57123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard this before, but I've never understood it. No, you shouldn't be forced to turn into a Solar. And you shouldn't feel punished for playing an Abyssal instead of a Solar. But why do you need moral validation of your character's decision to remain an Abyssal, in order to enjoy playing an Abyssal? I don't think you should get that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where am I asking for moral validation of my decision to remain an Abyssal? I'm asking that deciding to become a Solar should not be the only moral option. 2e really pushed the idea that as long as an Abyssal is an Abyssal, Resonance is eventually going to murder Creation with spreading shadowlands and rampant plagues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sin that an Abyssal needs redemption for is their assent to killing the world. But being an Abyssal is inextricable from that. If someone recants and says &quot;I won't be a world-destroying weapon anymore&quot; ...then if they walk that path to the end there's no way to continue to be an Abyssal, and they shouldn't even want to, because that's absolutely core to what an Abyssal is. Trying to &quot;repent&quot; without abandoning that path is like wanting to be a vegetarian without giving up bacon. When you say &quot;Yes, give me the Second Breath and I will kill the world&quot; the decision you make is not &quot;enlisting as a soldier for the cause of Oblivion&quot;. Sure, the Neverborn would prefer if you were on task, you'd be more efficient that way, but ultimately what is asked of you, and what you agree to, is becoming an Abyssal. It's the nature of the Black Exaltation: Will ye or nill ye, death shall ye cause. </div> </div> </div>Being an Abyssal is not about being a world-killing weapon. That's the thing the Neverborn want, but they got Solar Exaltations to work with instead. Being an Abyssal is about a lot of things - it definitely involves looking at the choice you made at the brink of death and answering the question &quot;what does this say about me?&quot; - but world killing is only a game for loyalists. There's a lot of dark attraction, a lot of the trappings of the tortured hero, a lot of flirting with death and its trappings. There's a certain allure to a blank check to be emo whenever you want to be. These are the things I should be allowed to play with if I want, but if I want to be a traditional hero I should not be forced to give all of that up and become a Solar. If I wanted to play a Paladin instead of a Deathknight, I wouldn't have bought Wrath of the Lich King, now would I?<br /> <br /> I want at least my third option and I'll take as many as I can get. Thankfully, 3e is going to be giving me what I want. Three cheers for the devs!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57282#post57282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, people are surely gonna care that they agreed to kill the World, I'm sure everybody will be totally convinced of the &quot;black spot&quot; you're talking about. But, just like in real life, it has no meaning because people aren't accauntable for their intentions, but for their actions. I see no reason why an Abyssal shouldn't laugh in the face of anybody who spases out over an imaginary thought-crime the Abyssal allegedly commited. So I really wouldn't like if the book spent pages, upon pages of content focusing on it and explaining how it's a Big Deal, when it's really not, the way Requiem spends way too many pages reminding you that life of a vampire sucks, when it should be awesome in it's own, special way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put it this way: If you are willing to murder the whole world with your own hands in order to either gain power or to save your own skin, you are a terrible person. If you see nothing wrong with this, you are an even worse person. Who cares what other people think? What do you think about yourself now? When you know you weren't lying when you said you'd do it? Are you going to go through with it? Are you going to hide from it, pretend it never happened? Are you going to try to change who you are? Your &quot;sin&quot; only matters to you, but it <i>matters</i> to you.<br /> <br /> Also, they haven't just committed a &quot;thought crime&quot;. They have committed conspiracy to commit murder a million times over.<br /> <br /> Now, you are right: The Abyssals book should focus on how awesome the things an Abyssal can do are. However, it should make a big deal out of this choice, because the choice is the part that says something about your character and who is is and where he is going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T00:38:40-08:00","id":57294,"title":"","content":"Attempts at subjective morality aside, there's nobody out there who's going to hear you agreed to commit omnicide and not think &quot;<i>Wow</i>, you're an asshole.&quot;. There's no system of personal ethics outside maybe of total solipsism that's going to say that's okay. And if you're laughing in someone's face about it, well then you're <i>really</i> an asshole.<br /> <br /> That said, it's self-evident. There's no need for the book to talk about it at length, or to punish you for it, because either you're sorry for it or you aren't. If you aren't, your &quot;punishment&quot; is how plotting omnicide rarely garners friends among the living. If you are, then your guilt is your punishment and ideally your reasons why give you some good characterization fodder. There's no need for some outside force to pass moral judgment on you, and doing so clouds the more useful point that how you feel afterward about your decision to become an Abyssal is foundational to what kind of character you're portraying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T01:09:56-08:00","id":57303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57293#post57293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me put it this way: If you are willing to murder the whole world with your own hands in order to either gain power or to save your own skin, you are a terrible person. If you see nothing wrong with this, you are an even worse person. Who cares what other people think? What do you think about yourself now? When you know you weren't lying when you said you'd do it? Are you going to go through with it? Are you going to hide from it, pretend it never happened? Are you going to try to change who you are? Your &quot;sin&quot; only matters to you, but it <i>matters</i> to you.<br /> <br /> Also, they haven't just committed a &quot;thought crime&quot;. They have committed conspiracy to commit murder a million times over.<br /> <br /> Now, you are right: The Abyssals book should focus on how awesome the things an Abyssal can do are. However, it should make a big deal out of this choice, because the choice is the part that says something about your character and who is is and where he is going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put it this way: it's not the job of the book to decide whether Abyssals are horrible or not. What I want, is simply for the book to present things objectively and then let people decide what do they think about it, not to bash people over their heads with moral preachings about how terrible people the Abyssals are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-25-2014, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T04:53:04-08:00","id":57361,"title":"","content":"Kyeudo, outside of certain religious views, where is it illegal to be coerced into being willing to kill someone out of desperation, <i>and then not following through with it</i>? <br /> <br /> People have foul moods all the goddamned time. Sometimes they're even willing to kill. But, as a society, we <i>generally</i> don't slap someone in irons for imagining stuffing a grenade into the mouth of that asshole who cut you off in traffic, and pulling the pin.<br /> <br /> As long as you come to your senses and <i>don't kill that asshole</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T04:57:24-08:00","id":57362,"title":"","content":"<b>Kyeudo</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57293#post57293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where am I asking for moral validation of my decision to remain an Abyssal? <b>I'm asking that deciding to become a Solar should not be the only moral option.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Um... you did it right here in the very next sentence? (Emphasis mine.)<br /> Look, an Abyssal is not a good thing. Which doesn't mean an Abyssal can't be a good <i>person</i>. It doesn't even mean he can only be a good person while or by trying to become a Solar. It does mean that the world with -1 Abyssal and +1 Solar in it would be a better place, all else being equal.<br /> But \u00aball else being equal\u00bb is a pretty useless hypothetical, so that's not really a big deal.<br /> If you want the game to agree with you when you say \u00abno, an Abyssal is a perfectly acceptable thing to be -there's no reason for me to want redemption\u00bb that's what I mean by moral validation.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57293#post57293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e really pushed the idea that as long as an Abyssal is an Abyssal, Resonance is eventually going to murder Creation with spreading shadowlands and rampant plagues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the mechanics were about as hamhanded as they could possibly be. But the intent was right. That's exactly what's happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57293#post57293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being an Abyssal is not about being a world-killing weapon. That's the thing the Neverborn want, but they got Solar Exaltations to work with instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Neverborn got what they wanted. It's the Yozi who are scheduled for a rude surprise.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57293#post57293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being an Abyssal is about a lot of things - it definitely involves looking at the choice you made at the brink of death and answering the question &quot;what does this say about me?&quot; - but world killing is only a game for loyalists. There's a lot of dark attraction, a lot of the trappings of the tortured hero, a lot of flirting with death and its trappings. There's a certain allure to a blank check to be emo whenever you want to be. These are the things I should be allowed to play with if I want, but if I want to be a traditional hero I should not be forced to give all of that up and become a Solar. If I wanted to play a Paladin instead of a Deathknight, I wouldn't have bought Wrath of the Lich King, now would I?<br /> <br /> I want at least my third option and I'll take as many as I can get. Thankfully, 3e is going to be giving me what I want. Three cheers for the devs!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with a lot of what you say -so much that I think we've been talking past one another to some extent. Actively going out to hurry up theworld-killing is the loyalists' game. I'm not saying that as an Abyssal you should be irresistibly railroaded into doing that. So in that sense I agree with you -options for everyone! But even if you don't do any of that you're contributing to the slow death of the world as a side-effect of whatever you're occupied with, by virtue of your nature as an Abyssal. That doesn't invalidate what you do. But it lends a certain urgency to those themes you mention in your post, which I think only heightens the interest of them. You don't have to <i>do</i> horrible things, but you have to <i>be</i> a horrible thing. What's very important to me is that the death-knight isn't just a palette-swapped paladin -the difference between Solars and Abyssals isn't just one of trappings. In light of that, and since I'm not quite clear on what you mean by a \u00abtraditional hero\u00bb, I'd like to ask you to clarify what you mean, possibly with an example.<br /> <br /> <b>FromBeyond</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57282#post57282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole idea &quot;Abyssal's purpose is murder and murder only&quot; is just mind-boggling. When I want to play a machine, I'm gonna play an Alchemical. And I'll have more freedom. There really is a better way of making people end up playing a bloodthirsty psychopaths then just forcing them to, don't let White Wolf convince you otherwise.<br /> <br /> Also, what moral validation? Don't push your morals down my throat man, if death asks me whether I will agree to kill the World for a second chance and I say yes, then it's really not your business whether it makes me guilty or not, so stop pushing this guilt and this &quot;sin&quot; on me. Jesus, just because you said something once doesn't mean you have to gloom over it forever.<br /> <br /> That's exactly the thing I hated about 2e Abyssals and it's not even becoming a bloodthirsty psychopath that bothers me, because I can get behind that, it's that I don't feel awesome while doing it. And that's the point- even if the game hinges on my realization that I will become a bloodthirsty psychopath at some point, then I want to have an incentive to do so, instead of being forced to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that you have to be a bloodthirsty psychopath, or a bad person, or whatever. And I certainly don't think the game should be trying to guilt you. I don't have any interest in mandating that everything must be gloom and self-deprecation all the time.<br /> The point I'm making isn't that promising to end the world makes you automatically a horrible person forever and ever. It's that <i>the promise wasn't an empty one,</i> and getting away from upholding it isn't as easy as saying \u00abI lied.\u00bb<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57303#post57303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me put it this way: it's not the job of the book to decide whether Abyssals are horrible or not. What I want, is simply for the book to present things objectively and then let people decide what do they think about it, not to bash people over their heads with moral preachings about how terrible people the Abyssals are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I just want the objective reality the book presents to be that Abyssals are inherently destructive to Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T05:20:14-08:00","id":57366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57362#post57362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that you have to be a bloodthirsty psychopath, or a bad person, or whatever. And I certainly don't think the game should be trying to guilt you. I don't have any interest in mandating that everything must be gloom and self-deprecation all the time.<br /> The point I'm making isn't that promising to end the world makes you automatically a horrible person forever and ever. It's that <i>the promise wasn't an empty one,</i> and getting away from upholding it isn't as easy as saying \u00abI lied.\u00bb<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree. I just want the objective reality the book presents to be that Abyssals are inherently destructive to Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ok, I can certainly agree with that. However, I think the implementation so far has been horrible. I feel like if the Resonance is to stay, it should target things that are exactly opposite to what you, as a PC, care about. Because then Resonance seems more reasonable, to an egoistic person. It seems like a small price to pay for power and an ability to protect the things that you care about, at the cost of the things you don't care about. But bit by bit, eventually, there will be nothing left in the World except you, the things you cared about and Resonance. THAT's an acceptable vision of Resonance. I can understand Resonance that kills the World around you, but I just don't get Resonance that punishes you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T06:27:59-08:00","id":57381,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm...<br /> <br /> This thread has reaffirmed my desire to actually buy and read Blood and Smoke.<br /> <br /> Entirely incidentally, mind, but still.<br /> <br /> Just as soon as the cycle turns over...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T21:36:16-08:00","id":57901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57282#post57282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, people are surely gonna care that they agreed to kill the World, I'm sure everybody will be totally convinced of the &quot;black spot&quot; you're talking about. But, just like in real life, it has no meaning because people aren't accauntable for their intentions, but for their actions. I see no reason why an Abyssal shouldn't laugh in the face of anybody who spases out over an imaginary thought-crime the Abyssal allegedly commited. So I really wouldn't like if the book spent pages, upon pages of content focusing on it and explaining how it's a Big Deal, when it's really not, the way Requiem spends way too many pages reminding you that life of a vampire sucks, when it should be awesome in it's own, special way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess this is the difference: I assume that Exaltations(2ed) are not fucking chumps. You do. I doubt there's any chance of reconciliation for these views, especially given that you don't seem to want to actually have a debate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57282#post57282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This whole idea &quot;Abyssal's purpose is murder and murder only&quot; is just mind-boggling. When I want to play a machine, I'm gonna play an Alchemical. And I'll have more freedom. There really is a better way of making people end up playing a bloodthirsty psychopaths then just forcing them to, don't let White Wolf convince you otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that, and would appreciate you not making horrible arguments and attributing to me. Or implying that I'm an idiot who can't think for himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T22:28:54-08:00","id":57914,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder how many of the people who are pushing for Abyssals as doomed and awful have actually played multiple qualitatively different Abyssals. I mean, I'm sure some of them have, but I'm guessing that <i>most</i> of the people who are into the idea in theory either do not play Abyssals or played one Abyssal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57294#post57294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attempts at subjective morality aside, there's nobody out there who's going to hear you agreed to commit omnicide and not think &quot;<i>Wow</i>, you're an asshole.&quot;. There's no system of personal ethics outside maybe of total solipsism that's going to say that's okay. And if you're laughing in someone's face about it, well then you're <i>really</i> an asshole.<br /> <br /> That said, it's self-evident. There's no need for the book to talk about it at length, or to punish you for it, because either you're sorry for it or you aren't. If you aren't, your &quot;punishment&quot; is how plotting omnicide rarely garners friends among the living. If you are, then your guilt is your punishment and ideally your reasons why give you some good characterization fodder. There's no need for some outside force to pass moral judgment on you, and doing so clouds the more useful point that how you feel afterward about your decision to become an Abyssal is foundational to what kind of character you're portraying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not actually clear on how much the Abyssals know about the &quot;kill everything forever&quot; deal when they sign up, but if someone came to me moments from my death, in the most distress I had ever been in, and said to me &quot;hey do you want to live forever and have superpowers? you have to kill everything if you say yes though&quot; I think there is a pretty decent chance I would say yes out of <i>intense emotional distress and desperation</i> and figure that I'll find a way to get out of it later. A lot of people's attitudes toward The Choice really seem like they're projecting the feelings they get about it as a player reading the book onto a wholly incomparable situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 01-26-2014, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T00:05:50-08:00","id":57952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57901#post57901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess this is the difference: I assume that Exaltations(2ed) are not fucking chumps. You do. I doubt there's any chance of reconciliation for these views, especially given that you don't seem to want to actually have a debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not sure what you mean by this. I don't think Exaltations are chumps, I don't know where you got that. It wasn't even a responce to your argument, so really, I'm confused. I can entertain a converstation, if you want to present the case for Abyssals as always-and-mandatory tortured anti-heroes, wailing in depression, by all mean, do so. I really want to see the merit of it and me not seeing it has nothing to do with Exaltations being chumps or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57901#post57901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said that, and would appreciate you not making horrible arguments and attributing to me. Or implying that I'm an idiot who can't think for himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry if you felt like I'm turning your argument into a strawmen. But you know, over the time I've seen people make the same arguments over and over again, so I'm speaking very broadly. Maybe too broadly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T02:51:41-08:00","id":57998,"title":"","content":"Resonance was kind of a half-assed system. The goal was for Resonance to force Abyssals to kill and destroy no matter what. So even if you wanted to be a good guy, you'd still have to kill and destroy stuff. Which, honestly, doesn't make Abyssals much different from most any other Exalted; I mean, I haven't seen too many Solars, Lunars, Sidereal or Dragon Blooded who are pacifists and refuse to ever kill someone.<br /> <br /> Really, when you're a PC Exalt in your average Exalted game, you're going to be killing people or destroying stuff at some point. So the idea of Resonance making an Abyssal have to kill people, honestly, just isn't a big deal. Why is a Day Caste Assassin &quot;worse&quot; for killing people than a Night Caste Assassin? Really, when you get down to it, he's not.<br /> <br /> So what Resonance currently is, is a bit of a clusterfuck. The Abyssal gets to pick what Resonance eruption he gets, so why not pick Stigmata? Now you don't have to worry about Resonance killing people. Ever. And at that point, Resonance stops being a particularly terrible thing and just something you check off. Heck, you can even use Resonance in positive ways, like opening up Shadowlands to help out your ghost buddies, or creating a positive intimacy towards a jackass mortal, just so you can kill them with a Resonance eruption and have no one be the wiser.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the fluff tended to present Resonance in a different way, implying that it was central to the Abyssal storyline and that it tended to destroy the things and people that Abyssals cared about. &quot;Oh, you care about that person? They're dead.&quot; We had people in previous threads try and argue that Resonance is so overwhelming in an Abyssal's storyline, that Abyssals should be unable to create or run kingdoms or organizations because anything they care about, or even just find useful, is supposed to be destroyed by Resonance.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Abyssals promising to destroy the world in exchange for power... eh.<br /> <br /> Literature and media is filled with examples of characters who make a deal with the devil, then give the devil the finger and go off to do their own thing. There's nothing terribly evil about promising to destroy the world in exchange for power and then, rather than destroying it, using that power to save the world instead. And yeah, Abyssals should be able to do that, presuming they want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T06:41:11-08:00","id":58061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57998#post57998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what Resonance currently is, is a bit of a clusterfuck. The Abyssal gets to pick what Resonance eruption he gets, so why not pick Stigmata? Now you don't have to worry about Resonance killing people. Ever. And at that point, Resonance stops being a particularly terrible thing and just something you check off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, look closer at what's really written in the abyssal book. While the player allocates the points to different variants of resonance eruptions, how and <b>when</b> it will manifest is in ST's hands. Who is encouraged to screw Abyssal over with those. And to veto player choices that are not likely to cause problems for him.<br /> So, in this case, ST can tell you that no, you <i>cannot</i> take Stigmata this time. Or decide that it will manifest as highly visible disturbing sentences appearing all over your skin. Right when you tried to sneak past those dragonblooded guards while pretending to be a completely uninteresting mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T08:36:51-08:00","id":58102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58061#post58061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, look closer at what's really written in the abyssal book. While the player allocates the points to different variants of resonance eruptions, how and <b>when</b> it will manifest is in ST's hands. Who is encouraged to screw Abyssal over with those. And to veto player choices that are not likely to cause problems for him.<br /> So, in this case, ST can tell you that no, you <i>cannot</i> take Stigmata this time. Or decide that it will manifest as highly visible disturbing sentences appearing all over your skin. Right when you tried to sneak past those dragonblooded guards while pretending to be a completely uninteresting mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is, again, why I said it's a clusterfuck. It's much more in the ST's hands, and depending on how vindictive he feels, or how punishing he feels Abyssal Resonance can be, Your can get utterly screwed over, in a way that's different from other Exalted. <br /> <br /> If your ST is part of the &quot;Abyssals can't control kingdoms or run organizations or have friends because everything they care about gets wrecked by Resonance,&quot; camp, then trying to play an Abyssal who is anything other than Soulfuck Killshitter is really, really hard because the ST will veto anything that doesn't totally screw over your character. If, on the other hand, your ST is more generous, then Resonance is barely a blip on the radar and, in many ways, even looser and less punishing than normal Solar Limit Break. <br /> <br /> Either interpretation, where Resonance is too restrictive or meaningless, is bad. That's why the Resonance rewrite rules in Shards were nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T22:00:29-08:00","id":58515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57361#post57361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kyeudo, outside of certain religious views, where is it illegal to be coerced into being willing to kill someone out of desperation, <i>and then not following through with it</i>?<br /> <br /> People have foul moods all the goddamned time. Sometimes they're even willing to kill. But, as a society, we <i>generally</i> don't slap someone in irons for imagining stuffing a grenade into the mouth of that asshole who cut you off in traffic, and pulling the pin.<br /> <br /> As long as you come to your senses and <i>don't kill that asshole</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Screw what the rest of the world thinks - you are the one who has to live with what you were willing to do. If knowing that you were willing to sell out the world to save your own life doesn't change how you look at yourself, you are already a sociopath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57362#post57362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... you did it right here in the very next sentence? (Emphasis mine.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not asking that being an Abyssal gets the Divine Stamp of Being Okay. I'm asking that the books stop ascribing a moral superiority to the state of being a Solar. I'm asking that the books stop considering being an Abyssal to be an offense against all Creation and a state that no one could ever want to be in unless they were a murderous sociopath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look, an Abyssal is not a good thing. Which doesn't mean an Abyssal can't be a good <i>person</i>. It doesn't even mean he can only be a good person while or by trying to become a Solar. It does mean that the world with -1 Abyssal and +1 Solar in it would be a better place, all else being equal.<br /> But \u00aball else being equal\u00bb is a pretty useless hypothetical, so that's not really a big deal.<br /> If you want the game to agree with you when you say \u00abno, an Abyssal is a perfectly acceptable thing to be -there's no reason for me to want redemption\u00bb that's what I mean by moral validation.<br /> <br /> I agree with a lot of what you say -so much that I think we've been talking past one another to some extent. Actively going out to hurry up theworld-killing is the loyalists' game. I'm not saying that as an Abyssal you should be irresistibly railroaded into doing that. So in that sense I agree with you -options for everyone! But even if you don't do any of that you're contributing to the slow death of the world as a side-effect of whatever you're occupied with, by virtue of your nature as an Abyssal. That doesn't invalidate what you do. But it lends a certain urgency to those themes you mention in your post, which I think only heightens the interest of them. You don't have to <i>do</i> horrible things, but you have to <i>be</i> a horrible thing. What's very important to me is that the death-knight isn't just a palette-swapped paladin -the difference between Solars and Abyssals isn't just one of trappings. </div> </div> </div>You are missing the point.<br /> <br /> The first and great commandment about a playable splat is thus: If someone chooses to play this splat, they should be able to have a fun play experience <b>as that splat</b>. The Abyssals broke this commandment in 2e. No other rule of game design or story trumps this one. If the Abyssal story is supposed to default to &quot;Sociopath or Redemptions&quot; they should never have been made playable in the first place.<br /> <br /> The Abyssals, as a playable splat, need to stop punishing players for not falling into the default molds. They need to assume that players will stay Abyssals for the length of their stories and that those stories will be diverse. The only way this works is if we ditch the idea of &quot;redemption = Solar&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sure, we should address the ramifications of the choice and what if means for the Abyssal who made it - I will fight you with knives before I see the choice go away. They should be constantly tempted to solve problems with death and violence (more so that Solars are). It should be a melodramatic experience and questions of morality should probably crop up a lot. However, it should never be a necessary thing to stop being an Abyssal or else they are not a truly playable splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In light of that, and since I'm not quite clear on what you mean by a \u00abtraditional hero\u00bb, I'd like to ask you to clarify what you mean, possibly with an example. </div> </div> </div>When I say &quot;traditional hero&quot;, I mean the classic &quot;I'm here to save the day and make everything right&quot; hero. If I want to play the Abyssal Lone Ranger or Abyssal Batman, I should be able to do it. I might have to pay a little more and do a little worse than if I used a Solar to make the Lone Ranger or Batman, but screw Solars - I wanted to play an Abyssal and ride a ghostly steed across the pale deserts of the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T23:17:39-08:00","id":58546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58515#post58515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Screw what the rest of the world thinks - you are the one who has to live with what you were willing to do. If knowing that you were willing to sell out the world to save your own life doesn't change how you look at yourself, you are already a sociopath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the opposite - if you are the person that is willing to <i>promise</i> anything (remember, <b>the will to go along with what you have promised is not a requirement</b>) to survive, then you are an average person, and definitely sane. The <i>only</i> reason why you might regret your choice later is because it's actually enforced.<br /> Not that there is a requirement for you to understand what you really agreed on - it's clearly said in the abyssal book, that while Deathlords must secure your agreement, and have to inform you about the main points of the deal, they can also lie, disassemble and muddle the issue. Nor, as i have already mentioned, are they required to make sure you comprehended what you were told.<br /> <br /> So, basically, no - just agreeing to the deal does not make you a bad person at all. Merely a desperate one.<br /> <br /> (i do fully agree with the rest of your points, however)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 01-27-2014, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T04:17:26-08:00","id":58623,"title":"","content":"Kyeudo- your priorities seem entirely contradictory. You say you don't want the game to put a stamp of moral disapproval on Abyssals and say that you don't want the books to explicitly tell us that Abyssal condition is something bad for being harmful to the World and then you go out and say that it should put a stamp of moral disapproval on Abyssals, for agreeing to kill the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T06:33:21-08:00","id":58665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58546#post58546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite the opposite - if you are the person that is willing to <i>promise</i> anything (remember, <b>the will to go along with what you have promised is not a requirement</b>) to survive, then you are an average person, and definitely sane. The <i>only</i> reason why you might regret your choice later is because it's actually enforced.<br /> Not that there is a requirement for you to understand what you really agreed on - it's clearly said in the abyssal book, that while Deathlords must secure your agreement, and have to inform you about the main points of the deal, they can also lie, disassemble and muddle the issue. Nor, as i have already mentioned, are they required to make sure you comprehended what you were told.<br /> <br /> So, basically, no - just agreeing to the deal does not make you a bad person at all. Merely a desperate one.<br /> <br /> (i do fully agree with the rest of your points, however)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that you aren't just anybody. You are a heroic mortal. You do have the will to go along with what you promised.<br /> <br /> Even if you don't realize that's what you agreed to initially, how long can you serve a Deathlord and not get at least part of the scale of what you agreed to do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58623#post58623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kyeudo- your priorities seem entirely contradictory. You say you don't want the game to put a stamp of moral disapproval on Abyssals and say that you don't want the books to explicitly tell us that Abyssal condition is something bad for being harmful to the World and then you go out and say that it should put a stamp of moral disapproval on Abyssals, for agreeing to kill the World.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want the people who agreed to become Abyssals to deal with the aftermath of their agreement to kill the world. I want them to answer questions. &quot;What does this say about me? What do I do about it?&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't want them being Abyssals to be the reason they are condemned. I want them to be condemned because of <i>who</i> they are, not <i>what</i> they are. I'm fine if Abyssals are dangerous and volatile and uncomfortable to be around. I just don't want the problem to be &quot;being an Abyssal&quot; instead of &quot;being a murderer of epic proportions&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T07:27:16-08:00","id":58696,"title":"","content":"If the character really is so full of hate and despair (or maybe just the serial killer type) that they really truly meant that they wanted to kill the world in exchange for their own life, sure. But if he/she was just feeling desperate at the time, or never really meant to follow through anyway, why should they be dealing with a moral dilemma like that? Not everyone in such a moment of desperation would agree, but a lot of normal people would. Yes, the Abyssal still has to deal with the fallout of the decision because other servants of Oblivion may be really angry and after him/her for breaking promises, but that doesn't necessarily mean the Abyssal should feel guilty about any of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1658-maelstromseeker","name":"maelstromseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T07:58:28-08:00","id":58712,"title":"","content":"I wonder...<br /> <br /> If it might not be better to present the agreement aspect of the Black Exaltation as more of a positive experience.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you give it enough thought, it seems somewhat contradictory to present the opportunity to stand as the eternal champion of Death under circumstances where death is all horrible and scary and something to be avoided, unless the intention actually is to cast certain aspersions on the character of the Exalt.<br /> <br /> I mean, it goes somewhat beyond &quot;make a terrible deal in exchange for power&quot; <i>and</i> &quot;make a terrible deal in exchange for staying alive&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it, I feel that the narrative surrounding Abyssal Exaltation has always treated it as though it was a lesser experience than it is. It's glorious transcendence into bodhisattva of eternal death, but it tends to be presented as, I don't know, joining Davy Jones' crew or something.<br /> <br /> No, no that doesn't quite cover it. Errrrr, that guy in Inglorious Basterds who sells out his fellow Nazis to not get killed? Something where there's some kind of collaborator stigma attached.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's not presented as that, but it's definitely treated as it by certain people.<br /> <br /> And Faustian bargains, but that never really seemed to match the actual circumstances, just the closest reference point in pop culture.<br /> <br /> Though I do think there might be presentations where it treats it like bargaining for your life, which is <i>really</i> underselling what you get out of Abyssal Exaltation...<br /> <br /> Or it would, except for the stuff that treats the Abyssal Exaltation as having sole utility as the tool you use to pay back your side of the bargain for your life, which... is not good.<br /> <br /> Anyway, should kind of be its own internally consistent thing, referencing the actual themes of Abyssal Exaltation (including how, even where death is cool, it's still death, and carries a lot of motifs that are at least threatening).<br /> <br /> So maybe not a positive or negative experience, but jeez, at least make it more about becoming Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T08:00:09-08:00","id":58713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57952#post57952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im not sure what you mean by this. I don't think Exaltations are chumps, I don't know where you got that. It wasn't even a responce to your argument, so really, I'm confused. I can entertain a converstation, if you want to present the case for Abyssals as always-and-mandatory tortured anti-heroes, wailing in depression, by all mean, do so. I really want to see the merit of it and me not seeing it has nothing to do with Exaltations being chumps or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how I got that? I read your posts.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57012#post57012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, most of them will start with a hell of an integrity boost- they've just cheated death and it didn't even notice they're selling bullshit to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:35:34-08:00","id":59012,"title":"","content":"Isator, I feel like I'm connecting with you on this. You can see what I mean when I say that I dislike Exalted's tendency to overshadow the awesomeness of the exaltation with the dark fate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58713#post58713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how I got that? I read your posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, let me clarify that. I don't think Exaltations are chumps, but it should probably be said that I don't think <i>Deathlords</i> are chumps, because you're not talking with the Exaltation, you're talking with the Deathlord, he or she is the one selling you the deal. Now, Deathlords being ages-old can totally see through you. they know exactly whether you're lying to them, whether you're just talking out of desperation and not really meaning what you're saying (which I posit to be the case among the majority of the people), or if you <i>really</i> mean that you're willing to destroy the World.<br /> <br /> Now. Do the Deathlords have a reason to give powers to people who don't really mean what they're saying, or are lying? That's the question we need to answer. And I think the answer should be &quot;yes, obviously&quot;, if the Abyssals are to be playable without limitting the character concepts too much. But why should they? Well, first of all, Deathlords don't have as much leisure as the Incarnea. They only pick from a very limitted reasource and most people simply don't understand the deal. And on a rare occasion they actually find someone who is willing, fully and knowingly? There are high chances that person is insane. Deathlords don't need lunatics, they need smart agents. <i>They need knights</i>. Secondly, Deathlords have certain specifications for their servants. It's very probable that the virtues of the individual will outwieght her unwillingness to cooperate. They might exalt someone over traits that have nothing to do with the end goal of their mission, because they are too useful to pass up on, such as great willpoer, cunning or things such as social position, wealth or knowledge.<br /> <br /> All those things can be much more useful to the Deathlords then conviction to the end of their mission. And finally- Deathlords work against each other. If one can get a higher ground with a servant that already dislikes another Deathlord, whom they also hate? They're gonna take that chance and run wild with it, whether the servant is going to be problematic or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-27-2014, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T13:27:39-08:00","id":59072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58712#post58712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder...<br /> <br /> If it might not be better to present the agreement aspect of the Black Exaltation as more of a positive experience.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you give it enough thought, it seems somewhat contradictory to present the opportunity to stand as the eternal champion of Death under circumstances where death is all horrible and scary and something to be avoided, unless the intention actually is to cast certain aspersions on the character of the Exalt.<br /> <br /> I mean, it goes somewhat beyond &quot;make a terrible deal in exchange for power&quot; <i>and</i> &quot;make a terrible deal in exchange for staying alive&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it, I feel that the narrative surrounding Abyssal Exaltation has always treated it as though it was a lesser experience than it is. It's glorious transcendence into bodhisattva of eternal death, but it tends to be presented as, I don't know, joining Davy Jones' crew or something.<br /> <br /> No, no that doesn't quite cover it. Errrrr, that guy in Inglorious Basterds who sells out his fellow Nazis to not get killed? Something where there's some kind of collaborator stigma attached.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's not presented as that, but it's definitely treated as it by certain people.<br /> <br /> And Faustian bargains, but that never really seemed to match the actual circumstances, just the closest reference point in pop culture.<br /> <br /> Though I do think there might be presentations where it treats it like bargaining for your life, which is <i>really</i> underselling what you get out of Abyssal Exaltation...<br /> <br /> Or it would, except for the stuff that treats the Abyssal Exaltation as having sole utility as the tool you use to pay back your side of the bargain for your life, which... is not good.<br /> <br /> Anyway, should kind of be its own internally consistent thing, referencing the actual themes of Abyssal Exaltation (including how, even where death is cool, it's still death, and carries a lot of motifs that are at least threatening).<br /> <br /> So maybe not a positive or negative experience, but jeez, at least make it more about becoming Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I grok what you're saying here and I mostly agree, but I'm not sure how positive the default Abyssal state can be cast without losing the narrative power of the choice to become an Abyssal. One of the biggest driving forces in Abyssal stories is their reaction to their own choice to become an Abyssal. Whether they stay loyal to the Deathlords or eventually rebel really hinges on whether they decide to go through with their choice or if they decide to change their mind. Without the questionable morality of that choice, what's the practical difference between an Abyssal and a Solar with an evil boss?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T13:53:29-08:00","id":59101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=57366#post57366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, ok, I can certainly agree with that. However, I think the implementation so far has been horrible. I feel like if the Resonance is to stay, it should target things that are exactly opposite to what you, as a PC, care about. Because then Resonance seems more reasonable, to an egoistic person. It seems like a small price to pay for power and an ability to protect the things that you care about, at the cost of the things you don't care about. But bit by bit, eventually, there will be nothing left in the World except you, the things you cared about and Resonance. THAT's an acceptable vision of Resonance. I can understand Resonance that kills the World around you, but I just don't get Resonance that punishes you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense to me too. If Resonance punishes every sin, then the Abyssal is trapped between Creation's rejection and the Neverborn's hatred. OK, so maybe she feels more allegiance to a Death Lord that way. But then the rebel Abyssals are totally alone in the world and the loyalists can be shocked with their pain collars every time they use the wrong fork. Great scheme for the bad guys, but terrible for anyone trying to tell a variety of stories.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'd much rather see Resonance as a corrupting force than as a destructive one. The puppy you pat on the head doesn't die in an agonizing fire - it follows you around, growing more protective, bigger, and meaner by the day. Your lover sees her rivals crushed by ill fortune and scarred by disease. Perhaps over time she craves your power or becomes obsessed with you, but she doesn't just die and turn into a zombie. Crops don't wither and die around you - in fact, fruit tastes sweeter and grain becomes more plentiful. Maybe the people who eat it change a little over time, or maybe they lose interest in fruit and grain, craving rare meat and strong drink instead.<br /> <br /> It's not like 2e Death Lords are all trying to shovel the world into a furnace *right now* so it's odd that their knights go around killing everything they touch. The subtlety of, say, the Silver Prince is kind of wasted when his lieutenants are forced to reveal themselves as agents of undiluted hatred for Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:08:15-08:00","id":59119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59012#post59012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, let me clarify that. I don't think Exaltations are chumps, but it should probably be said that I don't think <i>Deathlords</i> are chumps, because you're not talking with the Exaltation, you're talking with the Deathlord, he or she is the one selling you the deal. Now, Deathlords being ages-old can totally see through you. they know exactly whether you're lying to them, whether you're just talking out of desperation and not really meaning what you're saying (which I posit to be the case among the majority of the people), or if you <i>really</i> mean that you're willing to destroy the World.<br /> <br /> Now. Do the Deathlords have a reason to give powers to people who don't really mean what they're saying, or are lying? That's the question we need to answer. And I think the answer should be &quot;yes, obviously&quot;, if the Abyssals are to be playable without limitting the character concepts too much. But why should they? Well, first of all, Deathlords don't have as much leisure as the Incarnea. They only pick from a very limitted reasource and most people simply don't understand the deal. And on a rare occasion they actually find someone who is willing, fully and knowingly? There are high chances that person is insane. Deathlords don't need lunatics, they need smart agents. <i>They need knights</i>. Secondly, Deathlords have certain specifications for their servants. It's very probable that the virtues of the individual will outwieght her unwillingness to cooperate. They might exalt someone over traits that have nothing to do with the end goal of their mission, because they are too useful to pass up on, such as great willpoer, cunning or things such as social position, wealth or knowledge.<br /> <br /> All those things can be much more useful to the Deathlords then conviction to the end of their mission. And finally- Deathlords work against each other. If one can get a higher ground with a servant that already dislikes another Deathlord, whom they also hate? They're gonna take that chance and run wild with it, whether the servant is going to be problematic or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Exaltations canonically ask the same question if they are freed from Deathlord control. But, more importantly, you're essentially making a big part of an Abyssals Exaltation irrelevant, which is why I think it's making those Exaltations Chumps, just like the Infernal Exaltation in 2nd edition does for Infernals, and the forces of Hell. <br /> <br /> And no, I don't think it really limits options much. Or, rather, it limits them in a way that makes Abyssals a bit distinct from Solars, other than having a lot of black crap. Abyssals have made the choice between themselves and the world, and they have to face that choice. Otherwise, just make Solars and paint them black.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:12:58-08:00","id":59121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59072#post59072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I grok what you're saying here and I mostly agree, but I'm not sure how positive the default Abyssal state can be cast without losing the narrative power of the choice to become an Abyssal. One of the biggest driving forces in Abyssal stories is their reaction to their own choice to become an Abyssal. Whether they stay loyal to the Deathlords or eventually rebel really hinges on whether they decide to go through with their choice or if they decide to change their mind. Without the questionable morality of that choice, what's the practical difference between an Abyssal and a Solar with an evil boss?</div> </div> </div> </div>The choice can be significant without being immediately and overwhelmingly awful. It could be like borrowing money from the mob to win an election or *cough* cooking meth to leave your family some money before you die of cancer. At first the new mayor can use her political power to improve local schools. Maybe her mob contacts even give her information that helps cut back on violent crime. At first the meth guy can pay his medical bills and make sure his soon-to-be-widow can pay the mortgage. Similarly, the Abyssal might be allowed to turn his new strength against whatever he hated in life. The Death Lord gives him some training and sets him loose against the bandits that plagued his old village or the slavers that dragged his family away in chains. The Death Lord's goal should be to set that new Abyssal on a slippery slope: let him use his powers &quot;for good&quot; at first, but ask for seemingly innocuous favors and shield the Abyssal from full knowledge of the change he is causing. Maniacal gloating and liberal use of the pain collar might come into play later, but they probably aren't great ways to convince a new death knight to serve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:14:22-08:00","id":59123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59072#post59072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without the questionable morality of that choice, what's the practical difference between an Abyssal and a Solar with an evil boss?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shooting chains of ghostfire from beneath their skin, for one.<br /> <br /> Needing to do creepy death shit or murder people periodically to keep the walls from weeping blood for another.<br /> <br /> EDIT: More importantly, any moral dubiousness to being an Abyssal should be a more holistic thing, rather than come down to a single decision made at the start of their tenure that overshadows everything else they do.<br /> <br /> Like, following along with your Deathlord mentor should have more complexity than &quot;going along with your pledge to kill everything&quot;, even if they're generally villainous (also for more complex and holistic reasons than &quot;trying to destroy the world&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-27-2014, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:28:36-08:00","id":59140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59119#post59119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Exaltations canonically ask the same question if they are freed from Deathlord control. But, more importantly, you're essentially making a big part of an Abyssals Exaltation irrelevant, which is why I think it's making those Exaltations Chumps, just like the Infernal Exaltation in 2nd edition does for Infernals, and the forces of Hell.<br /> <br /> And no, I don't think it really limits options much. Or, rather, it limits them in a way that makes Abyssals a bit distinct from Solars, other than having a lot of black crap. Abyssals have made the choice between themselves and the world, and they have to face that choice. Otherwise, just make Solars and paint them black.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am of the mindset that putting too much focus on that choice limits Abyssals too much. I would much rather see them differented from Solars by the reaction they invoke from Creation. Also, what Isator says, I really think shooting chains rom your back is enough to make everybody sure that you're not a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T15:46:44-08:00","id":59217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58102#post58102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is, again, why I said it's a clusterfuck. It's much more in the ST's hands, and depending on how vindictive he feels, or how punishing he feels Abyssal Resonance can be, Your can get utterly screwed over, in a way that's different from other Exalted.<br /> <br /> If your ST is part of the &quot;Abyssals can't control kingdoms or run organizations or have friends because everything they care about gets wrecked by Resonance,&quot; camp, then trying to play an Abyssal who is anything other than Soulfuck Killshitter is really, really hard because the ST will veto anything that doesn't totally screw over your character. If, on the other hand, your ST is more generous, then Resonance is barely a blip on the radar and, in many ways, even looser and less punishing than normal Solar Limit Break.<br /> <br /> Either interpretation, where Resonance is too restrictive or meaningless, is bad. That's why the Resonance rewrite rules in Shards were nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but it's <u>Kill</u>fuck <u>Soul</u>shitter. <i>Get it right</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T19:23:28-08:00","id":59385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59217#post59217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but it's <u>Kill</u>fuck <u>Soul</u>shitter. <i>Get it right</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Killfuck Soulshitter was a Solar. Dawn Caste if I remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T19:31:54-08:00","id":59391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59385#post59385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, Killfuck Soulshitter was a Solar. Dawn Caste if I remember correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. His son, Spearpsycho Soulshitterson, is a Slayer. The family lacks an Abyssal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T19:52:11-08:00","id":59407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59140#post59140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am of the mindset that putting too much focus on that choice limits Abyssals too much. I would much rather see them differented from Solars by the reaction they invoke from Creation. Also, what Isator says, I really think shooting chains rom your back is enough to make everybody sure that you're not a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting too much weight on it is bad. But there's a bit of leeway between too much and nothing. And you seem to be committed to the &quot;it means absolutely nothing, unless you're crazy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T20:34:21-08:00","id":59434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59391#post59391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. His son, Spearpsycho Soulshitterson, is a Slayer. The family lacks an Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soulfuck Killshitter, Dusk Caste Abyssal, he could be an uncle... or a cousin...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T21:11:14-08:00","id":59466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59434#post59434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Soulfuck Killshitter, Dusk Caste Abyssal, he could be an uncle... or a cousin...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T22:23:24-08:00","id":59517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59407#post59407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting too much weight on it is bad. But there's a bit of leeway between too much and nothing. And you seem to be committed to the &quot;it means absolutely nothing, unless you're crazy&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want this decision to be a big deal for your character, great, you can have that. I simply object to it being a big deal for <i>every</i> character, mandatory, because I don't want the books to waste too many words on something that will be mostly ignored by 2/3 of my Abyssal characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:17:29-08:00","id":59552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59217#post59217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but it's <u>Kill</u>fuck <u>Soul</u>shitter. <i>Get it right</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was intentional. As an Abyssal, he kills shit and fucks souls.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T01:58:14-08:00","id":59645,"title":"","content":"A bit of a late reply here... I've been busy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58515#post58515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not asking that being an Abyssal gets the Divine Stamp of Being Okay. I'm asking that the books stop ascribing a moral superiority to the state of being a Solar. I'm asking that the books stop considering being an Abyssal to be an offense against all Creation and a state that no one could ever want to be in unless they were a murderous sociopath.</div> </div> </div> </div> But... it literally is an offense against all Creation. Spesifically, attempted murder. If you're saying you want that to change, then I think you're throwing the baby out with the bathwater. In my view that's totally core to the entire point of Abyssals. Never mind playable splat, if they aren't inherently inimical to Creation there's no reason for them to exist at all.<br /> <br /> I don't think you (should) need to be a murderous sociopath to want to be an Abyssal, however. You get enormous supernatural power, and you'll live for as long as the world does. Instead of a farm-hand or a soldier or a village doctor, you get to be a world-striding legendary warrior, and drink with ancient sorcerer-kings in obsidian palaces. It has its perks, is what I'm saying. That said, to choose an Abyssal Exaltation over a Solar Exaltation, all else being equal? Yeah, you'd have to be pretty morbid, or pretty insane. But there's that useless hypothetical again, which no-one in the setting ever gets, so it <i>doesn't matter</i>. As a player you're choosing who you want to play, not what you want to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58515#post58515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> You are missing the point.<br /> <br /> The first and great commandment about a playable splat is thus: If someone chooses to play this splat, they should be able to have a fun play experience <b>as that splat</b>. The Abyssals broke this commandment in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I played three Abyssals over the course of 2E, none of whom ever stopped being Abyssals, and I had three distinct fun play experiences... I do see your point, and I agree that the 2E conception of Abyssals got a bad, overly restrictive implementation, but don't say that it wasn't <i> possible </i> to have fun with 2E Abyssals, because people did. And I do maintain it was an implementation issue. I want something very close to 2E Abyssals in 3E, but better written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58515#post58515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No other rule of game design or story trumps this one. If the Abyssal story is supposed to default to &quot;Sociopath or Redemptions&quot; they should never have been made playable in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u00abSupposed to default to\u00bb? To the extent that they have an <i>iconic</i> story, like Solars can be said to have \u00abconquer the world, and try to avoid the mistakes of the past\u00bb, it is \u00abkill the world or do everything you can not to.\u00bb Which you could call \u00absociopath or redemption\u00bb, if you were feeling uncharitable, although the world-destroyer doesn't need to be a sociopath and the renegade doesn't need to ever turn into a Solar. But I've never seen a Solar game \u00abdefault\u00bb to world-conquering. And yes, at the theoretical limit, Abyssals have fewer stories than Solars within their thematic bailiwick. But that doesn't make them narrow in any meaningful sense. While you should be able to do many concepts in multiple different ways, there are some concepts for Solars that won't be workable as Abyssals, just like there are some that won't be workable as Sidereals or Dragon-blooded. Abyssals have their own stories, they're not just a different mode to play the Solar stories in. And it's not a bad thing that not all the Exalted types have equal scope for diversity, it helps give structure to the setting. Abyssals cover a more narrow set of character types and stories than Solars or Dragon-blooded, but no more narrow than Sidereals, and in my view, actually broader than Alchemicals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58515#post58515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyssals, as a playable splat, need to stop punishing players for not falling into the default molds. They need to assume that players will stay Abyssals for the length of their stories and that those stories will be diverse.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58515#post58515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The only way this works is if we ditch the idea of &quot;redemption = Solar&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is not. Why does redemption have to figure into the story at all, any more than every Vampire story has to be about Golconda? Heck, originally, redemption was presented as a rumor that might not even be <i>possible</i>. That ship has obviously sailed, but I have never understood why redemption is always front and center whenever there's an Abyssal debate. Be an Abyssal, deal with being an Abyssal, focus on what you <i>do</i>. It's probably going to be a story about death, and being cursed, and the relationship between means and ends. But it doesn't have to be a story about the destruction of the world, any more than a Solar story has to be about conquering or saving the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58515#post58515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, we should address the ramifications of the choice and what if means for the Abyssal who made it - I will fight you with knives before I see the choice go away. They should be constantly tempted to solve problems with death and violence (more so that Solars are). It should be a melodramatic experience and questions of morality should probably crop up a lot. However, it should never be a necessary thing to stop being an Abyssal or else they are not a truly playable splat.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why is it necessary? It isn't necessary! The story is about the character, not about the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=58515#post58515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say &quot;traditional hero&quot;, I mean the classic &quot;I'm here to save the day and make everything right&quot; hero. If I want to play the Abyssal Lone Ranger or Abyssal Batman, I should be able to do it. I might have to pay a little more and do a little worse than if I used a Solar to make the Lone Ranger or Batman, but screw Solars - I wanted to play an Abyssal and ride a ghostly steed across the pale deserts of the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure if you chose your examples very deliberately, but as it happens, both of them make for great heroic Abyssals! The Lone Ranger is the mysterious wandering stranger who shows up, helps the townsfolk, stops the villains -and rides away without allowing himself to make any ties. (In this case, to protect the villagers from Resonance.) Abyssal Lone Ranger is probably a bit less square-jawed,a bit more Man With No Name, and most likely not as careful to always aim for the bad guys' guns instead of their guts, but basically the concept is completely unchanged. And he still rides a pale horse. ;-)<br /> <br /> Batman fights injustice using fear and theatricality as weapons, preying on criminals' cowardice and superstition. The city he protects is a dark and gloomy place. His methods are sometimes vicious, but he restrains himself from crossing certain lines, for fear of going too far. And periodically he has to ask himself if his presence is contributing to Gotham's problems, causing escalation with his war on crime and acting as a lightning-rod to all kinds of psychotic villains. (The critical point here, with respect to the Resonance-analogy, is that <i>there is an element of truth to this, but Gotham is still better off than it would have been without Batman</i> -at least so long as he never fails. This is what allows both the Dark Fate and Abyssal Batman's heroism to be validated simultaneously.)<br /> <br /> Now by contrast, Superman and Robin Hood would be pretty difficult to do as Abyssals. Both of them are idols and protectors in a way that Abyssals really can't be -not without Resonance afflicting the things they are fighting for, and the means they have at their disposal tarnishing the ends they are working towards.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T03:33:10-08:00","id":59672,"title":"","content":"&quot;So. This is it. The end. In hindight, I should have seen it coming, that was a completely suicidal mission. I hope it worked. I hope I did everything in my power to protect my men, to protect their families. I hope I did everything to protect <i>my</i> family. I hoped I could see the end of this war, simle and look back and say: yes, we survived hell. Alas, that's not the fate that awaits me. Darkness. But no pain, only cold certainty. Will I meet my friends on the other side? Are they going to hate me, if it turns out I failed? I did best I could, didn't I? Maybe there was something more I could do. Maybe I could find a better way, if only I had more time, more strength. I wish... I wish I could do it all again... I just... I don't want to go...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Do <b>not</b> lie down yet, warrior- a mighty voice echose in the darkness, like a battle-ram, waking me up from deathly torpor. Listen to me general. Listen and judge wisely. You have failed and you are dead. You are powerless and you are left <b>alone-</b> so I did fail... However, the voice breakes silence again, <b>I</b> have chosen you, warrior. For your bravery in combat, for your devotion to battle, for your will to fight and protect. <b>I</b> have seen your skill and you have brought me much joy. For this I will bring you back. You <b>will</b> raise again, you <b>will</b> march again and you <b>will</b> serve again. But this time, <b>I</b> will be your Lord. Your family is <b>dead</b>. Your friends are <b>dead</b>. You can hear their voices, warrior, cursing <b>your</b> name. But you can live again. From this day, you shall be reborn as my servant. Decide <b>now</b> warrior, be the soldier of my cause, forever and ever, or <b>perish</b> here!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Listen to me, warrior- a voice like silken veil breakes the sielnce, it's soft but cold, like a soothing bandage. Do not fall asleep mighty warrior. Your mission is not yet done, is it? You have fallen, but it's not over yet. Merely a setback for one such as yourself. Do not give in to despair, for there is a chance. I can give you new life, a new chance to continue your fight. I must warn you however, if you are to accept, you shall become the pariah to your people, you shall walk the Lands of the Living alone, for you have become dead in their eyes. This is the price you pay and this is the only price you pay. You are strong. You are worthy. You are free. Raise now, warrior, and fulfill your dream. Decide now, live again, or perish here!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;... So <b>be</b> it&quot;<br /> <br /> That's my idea of how the deal works. Notice that in the second case, the goal is obfuscated. Deathlords, after all, don't have to be open about what it means to be Abyssal. And no living could trully understand what it means. The destruction of the World around them, is something that happens on its own. It might very well be, that it wasn't even an intentional implementation, after all, Deathlords are limitted in what they can do with raw Exaltations.<br /> <br /> At least, that's my preffered vision. If your Deathlord and you as a PC want to see it as a master-slave relationship? That's fine. You want it to be teacher-aprentice? Sure, why not. A rivalry of interest? That's fine to. Everything is subject to the particular case, there is no absolute. However, the rules of the Universe are what they are and they don't care. Creation rejects you, like an anti-biotic repels sickness, that is just a rule of the World. That is what Resonance means. You can't change that, but you can learn to live with it. How you deal with it? Now, that's entirely up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-28-2014, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T03:55:13-08:00","id":59680,"title":"","content":"I'm also going to reiterate my stance that it should be that, a lot of the time, you get Exalted regardless of how you answer the Deathlord's questions about what you would do in exchange for the chance to keep living.<br /> <br /> I feel like there could be something to that moment being a subject of introspection rather than a deal. Cause to consider how far you might go; that <i>anyone</i> might go. A moment to fixate on what death means for life, which might become something of a recurring question to an Abyssal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T07:32:11-08:00","id":59793,"title":"","content":"I'll just note that while my latest Abyssal <i>does</i>, in fact, serve under one of the Deathlords, he joined out of a sense that by offering Exaltation, said Deathlord saved his life, and thus my Abyssal owes him a debt of gratitude.<br /> <br /> He <i>wants</i> to <b>kill</b> the Deathlord, but first he's gonna have to pay off his debt, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T10:19:54-08:00","id":59929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59645#post59645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... it literally is an offense against all Creation. Specifically, attempted murder. If you're saying you want that to change, then I think you're throwing the baby out with the bathwater. In my view that's totally core to the entire point of Abyssals. Never mind playable splat, if they aren't inherently inimical to Creation there's no reason for them to exist at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then that is something that needs to change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think you (should) need to be a murderous sociopath to want to be an Abyssal, however. You get enormous supernatural power, and you'll live for as long as the world does. Instead of a farm-hand or a soldier or a village doctor, you get to be a world-striding legendary warrior, and drink with ancient sorcerer-kings in obsidian palaces. It has its perks, is what I'm saying. That said, to choose an Abyssal Exaltation over a Solar Exaltation, all else being equal? Yeah, you'd have to be pretty morbid, or pretty insane. But there's that useless hypothetical again, which no-one in the setting ever gets, so it <i>doesn't matter</i>. As a player you're choosing who you want to play, not what you want to be. </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'm fine with the fact that my continuing existence will eventually poison the world to death and that the people I care for most randomly drop dead.&quot; Really? You want to hang that albatross around the neck of any character that isn't on either the redemption path or the loyalist path?<br /> <br /> Also, every Abyssal gets the choice of whether to be a Solar or an Abyssal - that's what the current &quot;redemption&quot; is. The way it is currently presented, any Abyssal that finds out that they can choose to be a Solar if they try hard enough and chooses to stay an Abyssal is making the choice to kill the world a second time and this time there is no questioning whether they will go through with it or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u00abSupposed to default to\u00bb? To the extent that they have an <i>iconic</i> story, like Solars can be said to have \u00abconquer the world, and try to avoid the mistakes of the past\u00bb, it is \u00abkill the world or do everything you can not to.\u00bb Which you could call \u00absociopath or redemption\u00bb, if you were feeling uncharitable, although the world-destroyer doesn't need to be a sociopath and the renegade doesn't need to ever turn into a Solar. But I've never seen a Solar game \u00abdefault\u00bb to world-conquering. And yes, at the theoretical limit, Abyssals have fewer stories than Solars within their thematic bailiwick. But that doesn't make them narrow in any meaningful sense. While you should be able to do many concepts in multiple different ways, there are some concepts for Solars that won't be workable as Abyssals, just like there are some that won't be workable as Sidereals or Dragon-blooded. Abyssals have their own stories, they're not just a different mode to play the Solar stories in. And it's not a bad thing that not all the Exalted types have equal scope for diversity, it helps give structure to the setting. Abyssals cover a more narrow set of character types and stories than Solars or Dragon-blooded, but no more narrow than Sidereals, and in my view, actually broader than Alchemicals. </div> </div> </div>The default Solar story goes something like this &quot;The Solar Exalts doing something cool, then proceeds to deal with local problems that concern his character. He eventually fails to hide what he is and Wyld Hunts show up to kill him. In order to survive, he must either flee and abandon all he's worked for or gather allies, stand, and fight. This drags him onto the world stage, where he must make decisions that affect the fate of nations.&quot; Lots of variations on the central story and no fixed ending, but that's pretty much how it goes in every Solar game I've played.<br /> <br /> Abyssals currently have two default stories. The first is &quot;I'm a sociopath and so I help my Deathlord master kill the world, one piece at a time.&quot; This is not the game that most people want to play in Exalted. It can be fun to be the villain sometimes, but its not an all the time thing. The other is &quot;I'm a reasonably decent person, so eventually the constant murder and destruction gets to me and I rebel against my Deathlord master and seek redemption for my crimes.&quot; The second, inevitably, leads to being a Solar instead of an Abyssal and now you are telling a Solar story instead of an Abyssal story. Neither of these stories has much room for variations beyond which Deathlord you get to use.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals? They have more variation than anyone. What nation they serve, how much time they spend serving government interests vs their own projects, whether they breach the Seal or not - I could go on and on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is not. Why does redemption have to figure into the story at all, any more than every Vampire story has to be about Golconda? Heck, originally, redemption was presented as a rumor that might not even be <i>possible</i>. That ship has obviously sailed, but I have never understood why redemption is always front and center whenever there's an Abyssal debate. Be an Abyssal, deal with being an Abyssal, focus on what you <i>do</i>. It's probably going to be a story about death, and being cursed, and the relationship between means and ends. But it doesn't have to be a story about the destruction of the world, any more than a Solar story has to be about conquering or saving the world. </div> </div> </div>The thing with a vampire is he only has to live with assaulting a people to live. He isn't forced to kill his victims, he can choose to prey on criminals, and he's never, personally, a threat to existence itself by virtue of being a vampire. He can believe that he is a decent person.<br /> <br /> An Abyssal is in a whole different boat. He gets to watch as his very existence blights crops, haunts buildings, drives men mad, and kills those he loves most in horrible, painful ways. How do you live with this and still claim to be a good person? Especially after you agreed to this? Your only c<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why is it necessary? It isn't necessary! The story is about the character, not about the Exaltation. </div> </div> </div>Because the character isn't a loyalist and so doesn't want to eventually kill Creation? He wants to see his loved ones stop dying constantly? As long as Abyssals are an inherent threat to existence, they will eventually be forced to choose: Redemption-to-Solar or Loyalist-by-Inaction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure if you chose your examples very deliberately, but as it happens, both of them make for great heroic Abyssals! The Lone Ranger is the mysterious wandering stranger who shows up, helps the townsfolk, stops the villains -and rides away without allowing himself to make any ties. (In this case, to protect the villagers from Resonance.) Abyssal Lone Ranger is probably a bit less square-jawed,a bit more Man With No Name, and most likely not as careful to always aim for the bad guys' guns instead of their guts, but basically the concept is completely unchanged. And he still rides a pale horse. ;-)<br /> <br /> Batman fights injustice using fear and theatricality as weapons, preying on criminals' cowardice and superstition. The city he protects is a dark and gloomy place. His methods are sometimes vicious, but he restrains himself from crossing certain lines, for fear of going too far. And periodically he has to ask himself if his presence is contributing to Gotham's problems, causing escalation with his war on crime and acting as a lightning-rod to all kinds of psychotic villains. (The critical point here, with respect to the Resonance-analogy, is that <i>there is an element of truth to this, but Gotham is still better off than it would have been without Batman</i> -at least so long as he never fails. This is what allows both the Dark Fate and Abyssal Batman's heroism to be validated simultaneously.) </div> </div> </div>Now, what do Abyssal Batman and Abyssal Lone Ranger do when they find out that their very existence is slowly killing everything that is? Commit suicide?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59672#post59672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;So. This is it. The end. In hindight, I should have seen it coming, that was a completely suicidal mission. I hope it worked. I hope I did everything in my power to protect my men, to protect their families. I hope I did everything to protect <i>my</i> family. I hoped I could see the end of this war, simle and look back and say: yes, we survived hell. Alas, that's not the fate that awaits me. Darkness. But no pain, only cold certainty. Will I meet my friends on the other side? Are they going to hate me, if it turns out I failed? I did best I could, didn't I? Maybe there was something more I could do. Maybe I could find a better way, if only I had more time, more strength. I wish... I wish I could do it all again... I just... I don't want to go...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Do <b>not</b> lie down yet, warrior- a mighty voice echose in the darkness, like a battle-ram, waking me up from deathly torpor. Listen to me general. Listen and judge wisely. You have failed and you are dead. You are powerless and you are left <b>alone-</b> so I did fail... However, the voice breakes silence again, <b>I</b> have chosen you, warrior. For your bravery in combat, for your devotion to battle, for your will to fight and protect. <b>I</b> have seen your skill and you have brought me much joy. For this I will bring you back. You <b>will</b> raise again, you <b>will</b> march again and you <b>will</b> serve again. But this time, <b>I</b> will be your Lord. Your family is <b>dead</b>. Your friends are <b>dead</b>. You can hear their voices, warrior, cursing <b>your</b> name. But you can live again. From this day, you shall be reborn as my servant. Decide <b>now</b> warrior, be the soldier of my cause, forever and ever, or <b>perish</b> here!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Listen to me, warrior- a voice like silken veil breakes the sielnce, it's soft but cold, like a soothing bandage. Do not fall asleep mighty warrior. Your mission is not yet done, is it? You have fallen, but it's not over yet. Merely a setback for one such as yourself. Do not give in to despair, for there is a chance. I can give you new life, a new chance to continue your fight. I must warn you however, if you are to accept, you shall become the pariah to your people, you shall walk the Lands of the Living alone, for you have become dead in their eyes. This is the price you pay and this is the only price you pay. You are strong. You are worthy. You are free. Raise now, warrior, and fulfill your dream. Decide now, live again, or perish here!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;... So <b>be</b> it&quot;<br /> <br /> That's my idea of how the deal works. Notice that in the second case, the goal is obfuscated. Deathlords, after all, don't have to be open about what it means to be Abyssal. And no living could trully understand what it means. The destruction of the World around them, is something that happens on its own. It might very well be, that it wasn't even an intentional implementation, after all, Deathlords are limitted in what they can do with raw Exaltations.<br /> <br /> At least, that's my preffered vision. If your Deathlord and you as a PC want to see it as a master-slave relationship? That's fine. You want it to be teacher-aprentice? Sure, why not. A rivalry of interest? That's fine to. Everything is subject to the particular case, there is no absolute. However, the rules of the Universe are what they are and they don't care. Creation rejects you, like an anti-biotic repels sickness, that is just a rule of the World. That is what Resonance means. You can't change that, but you can learn to live with it. How you deal with it? Now, that's entirely up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got a great vision here. I'm not sure if your offers meet the &quot;must agree to kill the world&quot; bar, but this vision looks quite interesting. How do you envision Resonance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T10:43:40-08:00","id":59947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59929#post59929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got a great vision here. I'm not sure if your offers meet the &quot;must agree to kill the world&quot; bar, but this vision looks quite interesting. How do you envision Resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I like to think of Resonance as a by-product of Abyssal Exaltataion and something inherent to their being. It's best described as an intuitional reaction of Creation's Essence, actively decying and succumbing to entropy around the Abyssals. It's not that you're actively trying to destroy the World, it's not even that it's some kind of a ridiculous &quot;precausion methode&quot; implemented by the Deathlords to ensure the mission of their chosen, it's simply the effect of two different World clashing together. Like I said- anti-biotics fighting sickness. That's why it's called <i>Resonance</i>- a word used to describe disharmony caused by two forces meeting each other.<br /> <br /> Inherently, it has nothing to do with morality of your choice or actions- you simply belong to another World now. Reality sucks and doesn't care and the rules of Creation are what they are- you can be the purest of the pure in heart, but you are now something different that interacts in disasterous manner with the Realm of the Living.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, that's why I'm pondering the idea of helpful Resonance. Perhaps Resonance you can learn to limit or control, in similar way that Vampires learn to live with their condition. In my vision, mechanics that could allow you to target it. Or maybe it just works on it's own to help you. I think that when you get down to it, Abyssals have to treat the World as a limitted resource, the same way they treat food, for example. Would you rather have your loved ones eat, or people on the other side of the World, whom you know nothing about? Of course you'll choose your loved ones. So does it really matter that some people die, if you can keep people you care about alive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T12:56:59-08:00","id":60061,"title":"","content":"To me this is basically the essence of everything I want to be when playing as a Renegade Abyssal.<br /> <img src=\"http://24.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m8532tAhXi1qcoh8ko1_250.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://25.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m8532tAhXi1qcoh8ko2_250.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://25.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m8532tAhXi1qcoh8ko3_250.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T13:25:16-08:00","id":60083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=60061#post60061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me this is basically the essence of everything I want to be when playing as a Renegade Abyssal.<br /> <img src=\"http://24.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m8532tAhXi1qcoh8ko1_250.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://25.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m8532tAhXi1qcoh8ko2_250.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://25.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m8532tAhXi1qcoh8ko3_250.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, maybe it's just me not being a fan of the show, but I don't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T13:58:27-08:00","id":60109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=60083#post60083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, maybe it's just me not being a fan of the show, but I don't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I get : confronting your smug evil boss and telling him you're going to throw him out a window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T19:22:54-08:00","id":60321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=60083#post60083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, maybe it's just me not being a fan of the show, but I don't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the non-Angel character is a vampire, but I know he was a villain who did some bad things(not being intentionally vague there, just that I don't remember). Angel is confronting him, and the villain is basically saying that he's untouchable. So Angel asks the question, and then kicks him out a window(if he is a vampire, and I think the villain is, the windows had special treatments to block the sun, so that vampires wouldn't burn up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2005-cosar","name":"CoSaR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T20:00:44-08:00","id":60357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoSaR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=60321#post60321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the non-Angel character is a vampire, but I know he was a villain who did some bad things(not being intentionally vague there, just that I don't remember). Angel is confronting him, and the villain is basically saying that he's untouchable. So Angel asks the question, and then kicks him out a window(if he is a vampire, and I think the villain is, the windows had special treatments to block the sun, so that vampires wouldn't burn up).</div> </div> </div> </div>The best part is that most of the pilot builds heat for the bad guy in question like he's going to be the main antagonist for the season.<br /> He's a wealthy scumbag who uses his infrastructure to literally get away with murder in addition to being a vampire but then at the end of the episode Angel just punts him out the window like he's garbage.<br /> 14 years later it remains one of the most satisfying moments I've ever seen on TV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T20:56:58-08:00","id":60397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=59947#post59947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inherently, it has nothing to do with morality of your choice or actions- you simply belong to another World now. Reality sucks and doesn't care and the rules of Creation are what they are- you can be the purest of the pure in heart, but you are now something different that interacts in disasterous manner with the Realm of the Living.</div> </div> </div> </div>So one could avoid your concept of Resonance by staying in the Underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T21:45:34-08:00","id":60447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=60397#post60397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So one could avoid your concept of Resonance by staying in the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be fitting, don't you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T01:05:40-08:00","id":60554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=60447#post60447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be fitting, don't you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to consider it as long as the promises of a much, much cooler Underworld than 2e had are followed through on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T01:25:03-08:00","id":60561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=60397#post60397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So one could avoid your concept of Resonance by staying in the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose, but it's no different then current Resonance. The difference is that it doesn't make it impossible to go around Creation without breaking everything. But there is an assumption here that Underworld is cool enough that you'd actually want to be there for some reason. It has been problematic so far.<br /> <br /> However, I'm wondering if Resonance shouldn't rack up on it's own, even in the Underworld, just much, much slower. Because in the end, Abyssals are creatures of both Worlds. Unlike Liminals, who are somewehre between life and death, Abyssals stand fully on both sides. They're like Shrodinger's cat, both dead and alive at the same time and that's so paradoxical that the Universe rebels against it.<br /> <br /> There is an allure to life that lures them out of the Underworld eventually (best represented narratively, I'm not keen on solid mehcanics that would drag Abyssals out of their homes, seems too heavy-handed) and when that happen they will form bonds with denizens of Creation. It's inevitable, you'd have to be an amazing socipath not to form some bonds with the living. At that point Abyssal has to make a choice- try to contain their Resonance, through small sacrfices work towards making it into an acceptable condition... Or return to the Underworld and abbandon the living.<br /> <br /> It's good to make Underworld into a great setting in its own right, Creation is where all the shit is at. Abyssals need an incentive to actually interact with it and I feel like the current implemenation of this incentive (your boss tells you to, you either obey or you die) is horribly crude and uninteresting and it doesn't help that Resonance makes <i>you not want to do that ever</i>. There needs to be some form of middle ground here. On it's own, the idea of Resonance is sound, it's implementation that was butchered, as is with mostly everything 2e had to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 01-29-2014, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T15:28:21-08:00","id":61110,"title":"","content":"I generally disapprove of Resonance being a thing that inevitably kills the world because I disapprove of the state of being an Abyssal as a thing that inevitably kills the world. Emphasis on <i>inevitably</i>. My logic is thus:<ul><li>If you want to play an Abyssal, you should not have mechanics that urge or cause you to stop being an Abyssal.</li> <li>If Abyssals cannot stop being Abyssals, and Abyssals will destroy Creation simply by existing, then Creation is doomed and there's nothing anyone can do about it.</li> <li>You should be able to play Abyssals who are not destroying Creation.</li> </ul>The thing about Abyssals is that solving problems through violence and death should be the easiest solution for them most of the time, they can apply murder and manipulation of the resulting ghosts to solve problems that Solars can't solve that way. But making it so they have to destroy everything and don't get a choice in the matter, to my mind, takes away the more interesting dilemma of making the Abyssal choose how much they want to embrace that method, especially when it's easy and especially when they've already been confronted with their moment of weakness. Not everyone would have said yes to the deal you were offered, and you know it. In that moment, you valued your own life - not even your life as a whole, your current incarnation out of thousands that have been and would have been still - over the lives of everyone else in the world. Now you have to decide if you're going to embrace that dark part of you, if you hadn't done so long before you became an Abyssal, or if you're going to try to correct that weakness and become better.<br /> <br /> The choice is more interesting when you're constantly tempted to embrace that destructive side than when you're forced to destroy in roughly equal amounts no matter what you do. There are times you'll be able to justify it with relative ease, like when you kill a monster or a hated enemy. Then there are times you'll want to do it, but at the same time it will push your boundaries if you do. How far do you think you can go before you start sliding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T16:51:45-08:00","id":61157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=60554#post60554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm willing to consider it as long as the promises of a much, much cooler Underworld than 2e had are followed through on.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my very subjective opinion, Minton's write-ups for undead antagonists give you a way cooler Underworld than 99% of 2e's writing on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T19:24:11-08:00","id":61248,"title":"","content":"Another from my top 10 most Abyssal moments.<br /> <br /> This one courtesy of Gail Simone in Red Sonja 005 in which the antagonist Dark Annisia a former gladiator turned warlord talks with the spirits of those she killed in the arena and intends to kill more people to keep them company in the afterlife. There's ambiguity if she's insane or if she really is communicating with the dead but either way that's a very Abyssal way of dealing with the problem of &quot;I killed people because I had to and I feel bad about it&quot;. Certainly a very Dusk Caste solution.<br /> <img src=\"http://s28.postimg.org/sfzl254pp/Abyssal_moment.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T19:50:50-08:00","id":61252,"title":"","content":"I would be interested in the other 9 from your top 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:00:54-08:00","id":61257,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call it a &quot;moment,&quot; but Soulcatcher makes me think Abyssal pretty hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T21:48:49-08:00","id":61310,"title":"","content":"I'm going to keep to theme and follow up with another Gail Simone character, Jeanette the banshee from Secret Six.<br /> <br /> <br /> Jeanette is everything I\u2019d want from a Moonshadow. For the most part she comes across as an eccentric rich woman with interesting taste in fashion rather than an undead monster (though her reasons for being attracted to the assassin Deadshot are kind of creepy).<br /> <br /> However she holds a particular hatred of Amazons that becomes apparent during her fight with Wonder Woman where she starts getting scary quickly.<br /> I've had to be selective with frames here due to the image limit and some pages not being online (at least not that I can find).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://24.media.tumblr.com/93b858bd6c62ede13484217b58891954/tumblr_mvpomhxgep1r9uonxo2_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://24.media.tumblr.com/f01e55bf9e5813f7cb7fa8a59dfae72c/tumblr_mvpomhxgep1r9uonxo3_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/12/120267/3346626-7368983906-18540.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> More info: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I should probably explain the reason she hates Amazons because I think it works in an Exalted context.<br /> Jeannette died the first time during the French Revolution when her husband betrayed her and she became a Banshee at least in part as a result of a the botched execution, she's angry at the Amazons because in her eyes they abandoned the women of the world to suffer at the hands of men for centuries but more importantly they didn't save her.<br /> <br /> It could be interesting to have an Abyssal realise that their life would've gone very differently had the Unconquered Sun not turned his back upon Creation and have a lot of misdirected anger towards him (and by extension the Solar Exalted) because in a world that he apparently left to rot they had the audacity to pick survival over death.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-30-2014, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T20:26:31-08:00","id":62698,"title":"","content":"There were a lot of attempts to define what splat Bane was when Dark Knight Rises came out and for me this version of him was a Midnight.<br /> I knew he was going to kick the shit out of Batman the moment they announced he was going to be in the movie but that wasn't the part about him I found impressive.<br /> It was how in that first scene on the plane he sends a man to his death who goes with a smile knowing his purpose has been served.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0sCSsfaMfdE\" data-code=\"0sCSsfaMfdE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0sCSsfaMfdE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> It\u2019s implied that the fanatically loyal army he has in Gotham city was recruited from its disenfranchised. This is what Hardened Killer Training should be, the absolutely terrifying power where you know your minions will throw their lives away because you told them to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T09:14:09-08:00","id":63461,"title":"","content":"Hal Yorke, Being Human (UK).<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-3_9IkSL7Rg\" data-code=\"-3_9IkSL7Rg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-3_9IkSL7Rg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Hal's backstory has him explaining why he chose to become a monster rather than die on a battlefield and that he still hopes that he can be saved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yOjkNMHsx8s\" data-code=\"yOjkNMHsx8s\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/yOjkNMHsx8s/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> and more elaborating on his motivation and hopes for his redemption in a conversation with Mister Snow who is pretty much his Deathlord.<br /> <br /> Hal is such a spectacular cavalcade of Abyssal moments that I just went with the two I could find on Youtube.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T10:17:19-08:00","id":63485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=61310#post61310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to keep to theme and follow up with another Gail Simone character, Jeanette the banshee from Secret Six.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://24.media.tumblr.com/93b858bd6c62ede13484217b58891954/tumblr_mvpomhxgep1r9uonxo2_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://24.media.tumblr.com/f01e55bf9e5813f7cb7fa8a59dfae72c/tumblr_mvpomhxgep1r9uonxo3_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/12/120267/3346626-7368983906-18540.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate your list, but I'm a massive Wonder Woman fan and I have to comment on this.<br /> <br /> Wonder Woman has a lasso of truth, which you can plainly see she's wearing. She has that lasso of truth specifically so she can get people to give her information without threatening them or beating them. Yet writers frequently have her slapping people around for information. This drives me nuts.<br /> <br /> /end fanrant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T12:08:13-08:00","id":63531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=63485#post63485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate your list, but I'm a massive Wonder Woman fan and I have to comment on this.<br /> <br /> Wonder Woman has a lasso of truth, which you can plainly see she's wearing. She has that lasso of truth specifically so she can get people to give her information without threatening them or beating them. Yet writers frequently have her slapping people around for information. This drives me nuts.<br /> <br /> /end fanrant</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but sometimes, <i>you just have to slap a hoe</i>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">That's a joke, please don't hurt me.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T14:31:32-08:00","id":63599,"title":"","content":"I always saw the Lasso of Truth as something of a finishing move given that you can go &quot;tell me your secret weakness&quot; with it.<br /> <br /> Jeanette gets slapped around a bit but actually wins this fight with her Banshee Howl. Its not like Pants to be Darkened the unaired TV pilot where she tortures a guy in the hospital instead of using the lasso.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-02-2014, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T14:43:12-08:00","id":63601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=63599#post63599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always saw the Lasso of Truth as something of a finishing move given that you can go &quot;tell me your secret weakness&quot; with it.<br /> <br /> Jeanette gets slapped around a bit but actually wins this fight with her Banshee Howl. Its not like Pants to be Darkened the unaired TV pilot where she tortures a guy in the hospital instead of using the lasso.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lasso of Truth is a classic example of a writer 'oops' - and one that RPG writers might even take informative insight from!<br /> <br /> It produced like, how many good scenes before we were kinda... bored with it, and already knew what it did, and it wasn't a gimmick anymore?...<br /> <br /> ... and in turn, it -eliminated- how many other classic dramatic scenes, like beating people up for information or otherwise coercing them?<br /> <br /> Now replace 'Lasso of Truth' with 'Charm Of Your Choice' and you can see one of the unseen perils of charm design.<br /> <br /> The solution in this case is to politely ignore the lasso of truth. Coincidentally, this approach will ALSO work if you accidentally allow a bad charm in your game, as long as everybody is on the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T15:38:04-08:00","id":63621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/55030-3e-abyssals-are-dark-solars-a-conversation-from-the-tvtropes-forum-warning-loong?p=63601#post63601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and in turn, it -eliminated- how many other classic dramatic scenes, like beating people up for information or otherwise coercing them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every superhero needs to be Batman.<br /> <br /> Which could really be said as a matter for any superpower; I mean, part of the basic dramatic point of superpowers seems to be &quot;removing a basic weakness from the character so they can triumph in ways real people can't, and the story needs to find unexpected and creative ways to challenge them&quot;.<br /> <br /> One might as well say &quot;Superman shouldn't have heightened invulnerability because it removes classic dramatic scenes like flinching about and being at great personal risk while saving people from a burning building&quot;, when it would seem that being able to more effectively save people for lacking that risk is kind of the point of giving him the power in the first place.<br /> <br /> And even Batman has a character quality that removes the classic dramatic scenes of him killing people, so... there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T15:51:59-08:00","id":63626,"title":"","content":"Funny thing about the Lasso of Truth. The modern one is severely nerfed compared to Marston's.<br /> <img src=\"http://www.comics101.com/archives/comics101/images/2004/apr28/magiclasso.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Whereas these days it forces you to tell the truth, in the 30's it forced you to <i>obey her commands</i>, whatever they might be, because Marston was big into BDSM.<br /> <br /> Speaking of beating people up for information, the entire reason she had the lasso was to avoid scenes like that. In this time Superman was bullying gangsters and Bat-Man was straight up murdering them, to make Wonder Woman stand out, they made her <i>less</i> of a violent character. To put simply, it's a feature not a bug. No more a &quot;Bad Superpower&quot; than Clark's flight or invulnerability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}